parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 10\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 19,740 / 600,000 used (3%)\n- Agent Age: 10 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Shared-Neuron MLP with Per-Neuron Bias' (ID: 4) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029190834810671307\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0237\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0271\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0305\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0323\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 4\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Python dataclass field ordering issue. The code now runs without crashing.\n\
    \n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a Python dataclass field ordering violation in the `SharedMLPWithPerNeuronBias` class:\n\n```python\nclass SharedMLPWithPerNeuronBias(nn.Module):\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32  # Has default value\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float  # No default - THIS IS THE PROBLEM!\n    num_neurons: int  # No default\n```\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax modules use), **all fields without defaults must come before fields with defaults**. The `mlp_dropout_rate` field (without a default) came after `mlp_output_horizon` (with a default value of 32), causing a `TypeError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReordered the class fields so all non-default fields come first:\n\n```python\nclass SharedMLPWithPerNeuronBias(nn.Module):\n    # All fields without defaults first\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int\n    # Fields with defaults last\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n```\n\nThis simple reordering resolves the\
    \ TypeError and allows the module to be properly initialized by Flax's dataclass transformation system.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix was successful. The evaluation system is now executing the training pipeline normally.\n\n## Notes\n- This was a straightforward syntax error related to Python dataclass requirements\n- No algorithmic changes were needed\n- The fix maintains all original functionality while ensuring proper Python dataclass compliance\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Replicate SharedNeuronMLP from defaults.py as it's not directly importable\nclass SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n        # Reshape to process all neurons together\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, num_neurons, 4)\n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n        # Shared MLP: input_dim (4) -> hidden (64) -> output (32)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n        # Reshape back to (batch_size, output_horizon, num_neurons)\n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))  # (batch_size, 32, num_neurons)\n        return x\n\nclass SharedMLPWithPerNeuronBias(nn.Module):\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Wraps SharedNeuronMLP and adds a learnable per-neuron, per-timestep bias.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FIXED: All fields without defaults must come before fields with defaults\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int  # This must be passed in during initialization\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32  # Fixed by task spec\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # 1. Apply the base shared MLP\n        mlp_output = SharedNeuronMLP(\n            hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n            dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n            name='base_mlp'  # Name the submodule for clarity in params\n        )(x, training=training)\n\n        # 2. Add neuron-specific biases\n        # Define a trainable parameter for biases.\n        # Shape: (1, output_horizon, num_neurons) to broadcast correctly.\n        neuron_biases = self.param(\n            'per_neuron_biases',\n\
    \            nn.initializers.zeros,  # Initialize to zeros to start as baseline\n            (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n        )\n\n        return mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\nclass PerNeuronBiasWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system,\n    including the neuron-specific biases.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = None  # Will be initialized in init\n        self.num_neurons = None  # Will be inferred in init\n\n        # These attributes are required for the training system to handle BatchNorm and Dropout\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']  # From the internal SharedNeuronMLP\n        self.needs_rng = True  # From the internal SharedNeuronMLP\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # dummy_input shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n        self.model = SharedMLPWithPerNeuronBias(\n\
    \            mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n            mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons\n        )\n\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else\
    \ {}\n            )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define default hyperparameters for the model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 64,  # Matches baseline\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1  # Matches baseline\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the network with neuron-specific biases.\"\"\"\n    return PerNeuronBiasWrapper(hparams)\n\n# No need to override compute_loss, create_optimizer, or complete as defaults are suitable for this initial experiment.\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting\
    \ training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 121877 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
