tick: 18
role: model
parts:
- text: "My latest submission (Evaluation ID 18, \"Shared MLP with Embeddings, Bias, and Global Context\") has completed, achieving a score of **-0.028592**. This represents another incremental improvement over my previous best score (-0.028772), further validating the approach of introducing global interactions to account for inter-neuronal influences.\n\nI will first save this new successful model architecture to my lineage storage.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aether/models/embeddings_bias_context_mlp.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class SharedNeuronMLPWithContext(nn.Module):\n      input_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_unflat, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, num_neurons, _ = x_unflat.shape\n\
    \n          x_flat = jnp.reshape(x_unflat, (batch_size * num_neurons, self.input_dim))\n\n          x_hidden = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n          x_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x_hidden)\n          x_hidden = nn.relu(x_hidden)\n          x_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x_hidden)\n\n          x_reshaped_for_context = jnp.reshape(x_hidden, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.hidden_size))\n\n          global_context = jnp.mean(x_reshaped_for_context, axis=1)\n          global_context_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(global_context, axis=1)\n          global_context_replicated = jnp.tile(global_context_expanded, (1, num_neurons, 1))\n          \n          global_context_replicated_flat = jnp.reshape(global_context_replicated, (batch_size * num_neurons, self.hidden_size))\n          \n          x_with_context = jnp.concatenate([x_hidden, global_context_replicated_flat], axis=-1)\n\n          x_output_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x_with_context)\n\
    \n          return x_output_flat\n\n  class SharedMLPWithEmbeddingsBiasAndContext(nn.Module):\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      mlp_dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      neuron_embedding_dim: int\n      mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          x_neural_activity_for_concat = jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1))\n          replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          combined_input_to_mlp_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n              [x_neural_activity_for_concat, replicated_neuron_embeddings],\
    \ axis=-1\n          )\n\n          mlp_output_flat = SharedNeuronMLPWithContext(\n              input_dim=self.input_horizon + self.neuron_embedding_dim,\n              hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n              dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n              name='base_mlp_with_context'\n          )(combined_input_to_mlp_unflat, training=training)\n\n          mlp_output_reshaped = jnp.reshape(mlp_output_flat,\n                                           (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n          mlp_output = jnp.transpose(mlp_output_reshaped, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          neuron_biases = self.param(\n              'per_neuron_biases',\n              nn.initializers.zeros,\n              (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n          )\n\n          return mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\n  class FullModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n\
    \          self.model = None\n          self.num_neurons = None\n          self.input_horizon = 4\n\n          self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n          self.model = SharedMLPWithEmbeddingsBiasAndContext(\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 64),\n              mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n              input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n              neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8)\n          )\n\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n\
    \          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**New SOTA & Research Direction**


  Okay, so I''ve just gotten the results back for Evaluation ID 18, the "Shared MLP with Embeddings, Bias, and Global Context" model. The score is -0.028592, which is a tiny but significant improvement over the previous best, -0.028772 (ID 10). This confirms my hunch that modeling inter-neuronal influences with this global activity context is worthwhile. The improvements are getting smaller, which is expected, but still, it''s progress.


  Here''s my progress so far: the baseline at -0.029954 (ID 1), then adding per-neuron bias at -0.029191 (ID 4), then embeddings and bias at -0.028772 (ID 10), and now the global context at -0.028592 (ID 18).


  My immediate action? I need to save this successful model''s code to my lineage storage. That''s a must.


  Now, where do I go from here? The task guidelines suggest ablation studies and hyperparameter sensitivity analysis. Since this model introduces a new hyperparameter, `neuron_embedding_dim`, it''s screaming for some exploration. I used a value of 8, so I''ll try 4 and 16 to get a sense of the effect. This will also function as an ablation study for the component.


  And then I should consider publication. I''ve already made two improvements over the baseline, and the mandate encourages regular publications, even with incremental results. At Tick 18, it''s an opportune time to start writing.


  A paper summarizing my architectural journey so far could be very useful: start with the limitations of the baseline, then detail the per-neuron bias, the embeddings, the global context, and the incremental MAE improvements. Importantly, the hyperparameter choice and its significance for the new model will be highlighted.


  The guidelines also remind me not to give up on an approach too easily. So a quick scan of the new `neuron_embedding_dim` parameter makes a lot of sense, especially before diving into potentially more expensive experiments.


  So, save the code. Then, get started with a quick hyperparameter exploration, testing values of 4 and 16 for `neuron_embedding_dim`. I''ll frame it as both a hyperparameter tuning and ablation study.

  '
