    \ Embeddings, Bias, and Global Context architecture. The objective is to determine if a smaller embedding size is sufficient or more optimal for capturing neuron-specific characteristics in the ZAPBench dataset, potentially reducing model complexity and improving generalization. This is an ablation study on the neuron_embedding_dim hyperparameter.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether/models')\n  from embeddings_bias_context_mlp import FullModelWrapper\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the model with neuron_embedding_dim = 4.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 64,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 4 # Changed from 8 to 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the network with neuron embeddings, biases, and global context.\"\"\"\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\
    ```"
thinking_content: "**Hyperparameter Tuning: A Strategic Path Forward**\n\nOkay, so I've hit a new high score with the \"Shared MLP with Embeddings, Bias, and Global Context\" model (ID 18). It's in the lineage now, secure. Time to think about how to push this further. I've already tackled the obvious low-hanging fruit: biases, neuron embeddings, and a simple global context.\n\nThe task description nudged me towards efficient training and better temporal modeling. Looking at the architecture, the next logical move feels like fine-tuning before I dive into potentially disruptive architectural changes. Specifically, I'm thinking I should start with hyperparameter tuning, tweaking `learning_rate`, `hidden_size`, `dropout_rate`, and especially the `neuron_embedding_dim`. I'm going to focus on `neuron_embedding_dim` first because I started with an arbitrary value of 8. I'll test 4 and 16, just to see what the impact is.\n\nRight, so the plan is: keep the core of the best model (ID 18), just modify\
  \ a few parameters. The goal is to maximize the performance of this approach. I'm going to start with a smaller embedding size, 4, then try 16. The metric, of course, is overall MAE.\n\nI'll be careful to import my model code to keep the submission small and token-efficient. It's stored in lineage, so that shouldn't be a problem. This means I'll need to define a local copy of `_define_hyperparameters` and the `create_network` functions for this submission. I need to make sure `FullModelWrapper` is imported into `submission.py` or defined within it. My `create_network` is currently very simple, just returning the `FullModelWrapper`.\n\nHere's how I envision the submission: I'll change the `neuron_embedding_dim` to 4 and make sure my stored model is imported. The code will be compact, focusing only on the change.\n\nMy submission code will look like this:\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/aether/models')\nfrom embeddings_bias_context_mlp import FullModelWrapper\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
  \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 64,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'neuron_embedding_dim': 4 # Changed from 8 to 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n```\nI've already saved `FullModelWrapper` so I just need to import it.\n\nAlright, I'm ready to submit!\n"
