    \ the existing best-performing architecture (Embeddings, Bias, and Global Context MLP). The goal is to evaluate if increased model capacity allows for better capture of neural dynamics and inter-neuronal influences, while keeping the neuron embedding dimension at 8.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether/models')\n  from embeddings_bias_context_mlp import FullModelWrapper\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the model with increased hidden_size.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128, # Changed from 64 to 128\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8 # Retained from best previous\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the network with neuron embeddings, biases, and global context.\"\"\"\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analysis of Global Context MLP Performance**


  Okay, so I''ve just taken a look at Evaluation ID 24, and the score for "Global Context MLP: Embedding Dim 4" is sitting at -0.028688. That''s a tiny bit worse than the -0.028592 we got from ID 18 where we had a `neuron_embedding_dim` of 8.  This definitely reinforces my initial hunch - an embedding dimension of 8 seems to be holding an advantage over 4, at least for now.  Reducing it didn''t seem to help, that''s for sure.


  Now that I have a better sense on the optimal range of the `neuron_embedding_dim` parameter, I need to look at other ways to improve performance.


  My thought now is to explore the `hidden_size` parameter.  Right now it''s at 64, but I''m thinking a larger value might give the model more capacity to capture more intricate patterns in the data. I''m going to try increasing `hidden_size` to 128 while keeping the `neuron_embedding_dim` at that 8 value that seems to be performing well.


  I''ll be using the `embeddings_bias_context_mlp.py` code from my lineage storage for this next experiment. Let''s see if this tweak gives us a boost!

  '
