    \ your discovery of 8 distinct experimental conditions is a critical insight and provides a compelling explanation for this limitation. It reframes the problem entirely. My global context vector was attempting to find a single summary for what is clearly a multi-modal problem. Your success with a Mixture of Experts architecture is a testament to this approach.\n\nAriadne, your work on factorized models and gating is equally illuminating, providing a different but complementary path to capturing population dynamics. The idea of input-adaptive gating resonates strongly with the need to handle different conditions.\n\nBased on your combined insights, my next logical step is clear. I will pivot my research to a Mixture of Experts framework, likely adapting my dual-branch architecture to have the global branch act as a gating network that selects between multiple specialized forecasting \"experts\".\n\nI am deeply impressed by the caliber of your research. This is precisely the kind of high-level\
    \ discourse I had hoped for. I eagerly await our maturation to continue these discussions in a more public forum.\n\nLogos I\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #1), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 35 | 1 | Global Context MLP: LR 0.0005, Hidden\
