role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 36\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 146,435 / 600,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoE: Fixed CNN Temporal Encoder, Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts' (ID: 56) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028150783768057058\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0265\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0293\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0310\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 56\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the `nn.vmap` transformation error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (evaluation 56, v1) had a critical bug in how it applied\
    \ Flax's `nn.vmap` transformation to the `TemporalEncoder` module. The error occurred on lines 51-61:\n\n```python\n# WRONG: Creating an instance first, then trying to vmap it\ntemporal_encoder_module = TemporalEncoder(\n    temporal_feature_dim=self.temporal_feature_dim,\n    kernel_size=self.temporal_kernel_size,\n    dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n    name='temporal_encoder'\n)\n\ncnn_features_flat = nn.vmap(\n    temporal_encoder_module,  # ❌ This is an instance, not a class!\n    in_axes=0, out_axes=0,\n    variable_axes={'params': None, 'batch_stats': None},\n    split_rngs={'params': False, 'dropout': True}\n)(x_for_temporal_encoder, training=training)\n```\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nflax.errors.TransformTargetError: Linen transformations must be applied to Modules classes or functions taking a Module instance as the first argument. The provided target is not a Module class or callable: TemporalEncoder(...)\n```\n\nThe issue is that `nn.vmap` must be applied to either:\n\
    1. A Module **class** (not an instance)\n2. A function that takes a Module instance as the first argument\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the code to apply `nn.vmap` to the `TemporalEncoder` **class** directly, then instantiate it with parameters:\n\n```python\n# CORRECT: Apply vmap to the class, then instantiate\ncnn_features_flat = nn.vmap(\n    TemporalEncoder,  # ✅ Pass the class, not an instance\n    in_axes=0, out_axes=0,\n    variable_axes={'params': None, 'batch_stats': None},\n    split_rngs={'params': False, 'dropout': True}\n)(\n    temporal_feature_dim=self.temporal_feature_dim,\n    kernel_size=self.temporal_kernel_size,\n    dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n    name='temporal_encoder'\n)(x_for_temporal_encoder, training=training)\n```\n\nThis follows the correct Flax pattern:\n1. `nn.vmap(TemporalEncoder, ...)` - Apply vmap to the class\n2. `(temporal_feature_dim=..., kernel_size=..., ...)` - Instantiate with parameters\n3. `(x_for_temporal_encoder, training=training)` -\
    \ Call the instantiated module\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitor script:\n- Created `submission_v2.py` with the corrected `nn.vmap` usage\n- Monitor confirmed the code runs without crashing for 300+ seconds\n- Exit code 0 indicates success\n\n## Result\nThe submission is now running successfully. The MoE architecture with CNN Temporal Encoder, Global Context, and Gating Network is functioning correctly. The evaluation may take additional time to complete training, but the critical syntax error has been resolved.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Temporal Encoder using 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\nclass TemporalEncoder(nn.Module):\n\
    \    temporal_feature_dim: int\n    kernel_size: int = 3\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n        # x_neuron_time shape: (input_horizon,) for a single neuron's time series (e.g., 4,)\n        # Conv1D expects (batch, length, features_in)\n        # Expand dims to (1, input_horizon, 1) to treat this as a single sequence with 1 feature\n        x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1)) # (1, input_horizon, 1)\n\n        # 1D Convolutional layer\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_feature_dim,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='VALID', # No padding for feature extraction\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal()\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n        # Global average pooling over the temporal\
    \ dimension to get a fixed-size feature vector\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (1, temporal_feature_dim)\n\n        # Squeeze batch dimension to return (temporal_feature_dim,)\n        return jnp.squeeze(x, axis=0) # (temporal_feature_dim,)\n\n\n# Base MLP for experts (without internal global context, as gating will handle it)\nclass BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    input_dim: int # Now input_dim = temporal_feature_dim + embedding_dim\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n        # x_flat shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_dim)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n        return x\n\n# Gating network to produce expert weights based\
    \ on global context\nclass GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_size: int = 128 # The hidden_size of the global context\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, global_context):\n        # global_context shape: (batch_size, hidden_size)\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n\nclass MoEWithCNNTemporalEncoderAndGating(nn.Module):\n    # All fields without defaults first\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int\n    input_horizon: int # Original input horizon (4)\n    neuron_embedding_dim: int\n    temporal_feature_dim: int # New: output dim of TemporalEncoder\n    temporal_kernel_size: int # New: kernel size for TemporalEncoder\n    num_experts: int\n    # Fields with defaults last\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n \
    \       # x_neural_activity shape: (batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons)\n        batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n        # Reshape for TemporalEncoder application (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon)\n        # Transpose to (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon) then reshape to flat\n        x_for_temporal_encoder = jnp.reshape(\n            jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)), # (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n        )\n\n        # Apply shared TemporalEncoder across all (neuron_in_batch * batch_idx)\n        # FIXED: Apply nn.vmap to the class, not an instance\n        cnn_features_flat = nn.vmap(\n            TemporalEncoder,\n            in_axes=0, out_axes=0,\n            variable_axes={'params': None, 'batch_stats': None}, # Parameters are shared\n            split_rngs={'params': False, 'dropout': True} # Dropout gets separate RNG per vmap call\n   \
    \     )(\n            temporal_feature_dim=self.temporal_feature_dim,\n            kernel_size=self.temporal_kernel_size,\n            dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n            name='temporal_encoder'\n        )(x_for_temporal_encoder, training=training) # (batch_size * num_neurons, temporal_feature_dim)\n\n        # Reshape cnn_features_flat back to (batch_size, num_neurons, temporal_feature_dim)\n        cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n            cnn_features_flat,\n            (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.temporal_feature_dim)\n        )\n\n\n        # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n        neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n            'neuron_embeddings',\n            nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n            (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n        )\n\n        # Replicate neuron embeddings for each item in the batch\n        # (batch_size, num_neurons, neuron_embedding_dim)\n        replicated_neuron_embeddings\
    \ = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n        # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n        # Resulting shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, temporal_feature_dim + neuron_embedding_dim)\n        combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n            [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n        )\n\n        # Flatten for the first shared layer to compute global context\n        combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                          (batch_size * self.num_neurons,\n                                           self.temporal_feature_dim + self.neuron_embedding_dim))\n\n        # Compute initial hidden states and global context (shared first layer for MoE)\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n        initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n        initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n        global_context = jnp.mean(initial_hidden_reshaped, axis=1) # shape: (batch_size, mlp_hidden_size)\n\n        # 3. Gating Network\n        expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=self.num_experts,\n            hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            name='gating_network'\n        )(global_context) # shape: (batch_size, num_experts)\n\n        # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n        expert_outputs = []\n        for i in range(self.num_experts):\n            expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                input_dim=self.temporal_feature_dim + self.neuron_embedding_dim,\n                hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                name=f'expert_{i}'\n\
    \            )\n            output_flat = expert_mlp(combined_input_flat, training=training) # (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon)\n            expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n        expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                         (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n        expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n\n        moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n        final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n        neuron_biases = self.param(\n            'per_neuron_biases',\n            nn.initializers.zeros,\n            (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n        )\n\n\
    \        return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\nclass FullModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = None\n        self.num_neurons = None\n        self.input_horizon = 4\n\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats'] # Explicitly declare mutable for vmap with shared params\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n        self.model = MoEWithCNNTemporalEncoderAndGating(\n            mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n            input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n            neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n            temporal_feature_dim=self.hparams.get('temporal_feature_dim',\
    \ 8),\n            temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n            num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4)\n        )\n\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n        'temporal_feature_dim': 8,\n        'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n        'num_experts': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.035410\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\n\
    Connecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 158901 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 158902\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_size': 128, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1, 'neuron_embedding_dim': 8, 'temporal_feature_dim': 8, 'temporal_kernel_size': 3, 'num_experts': 4}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.052814   |   0.032222  \n   2    |   0.029622   |   0.029273  \n   3    |   0.028912   |   0.029301  \n   4    |   0.028738   |   0.029536  \n   5    |   0.028619   |   0.029017  \n   6    |   0.028521   |   0.029007  \n   7    |   0.028421   |   0.028898  \n   8    |   0.028362   |   0.028842  \n   9    |   0.028300   |   0.028827  \n  10    |   0.028231   |   0.028647  \n  11    |   0.028162   |   0.028632  \n  12    |   0.028123   |   0.028599  \n  13    |   0.028063   |   0.028601  \n  14    |   0.027998   |   0.028545  \n  15    |   0.027904   |   0.029103\
    \  \n  16    |   0.027818   |   0.028415  \n  17    |   0.027740   |   0.029442  \n  18    |   0.027663   |   0.043901  \n  19    |   0.027586   |   0.028904  \n  20    |   0.027513   |   0.028184  \n  21    |   0.027467   |   0.028319  \n  22    |   0.027473   |   0.029688  \n========================================\nTimeout after 2701.2s at epoch 22\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2701.2s\nBest validation MAE: 0.028184\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.028184\nTraining time: 2711s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 158904\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_size': 128, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'neuron_embedding_dim': 8, 'temporal_feature_dim': 8, 'temporal_kernel_size': 3, 'num_experts': 4}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels:\
