role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 48\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,918 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 48 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoE: Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1' (ID: 84) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027839121678215683\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0262\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0288\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0309\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 84\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code in version 3. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 84) had two critical errors:\n\
    \n### Error 1: Dataclass Field Ordering (Fixed in v2)\nIn the `TemporalFeatureExtractor` class, a non-default argument (`input_horizon`) was placed after fields with default values (`kernel_size`, `dropout_rate`). This violates Python's dataclass rules, which Flax modules enforce.\n\n**Original code (lines 10-13):**\n```python\nclass TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    temporal_conv_channels: int  # No default\n    kernel_size: int = 3          # Has default\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1     # Has default\n    input_horizon: int            # No default - ERROR!\n```\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nTypeError: non-default argument 'input_horizon' follows default argument\n```\n\n### Error 2: Incorrect nn.vmap Usage (Fixed in v3)\nThe code attempted to use `nn.vmap` with an instantiated module instance, but Flax's `nn.vmap` expects a module class or callable, not an instance.\n\n**Problematic code (v2, lines 91-104):**\n```python\ntemporal_extractor_module = TemporalFeatureExtractor(...)\
    \  # Instance created\ncnn_features_flat = nn.vmap(\n    temporal_extractor_module,  # ERROR: passing instance, not class\n    ...\n)(x_for_temporal_extractor, training=training)\n```\n\n**Error message:**\n```\nflax.errors.TransformTargetError: Linen transformations must be applied to Modules classes or functions taking a Module instance as the first argument. The provided target is not a Module class or callable\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix v2 (Partial)\nMoved `input_horizon` field before the fields with default values:\n```python\nclass TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    temporal_conv_channels: int\n    input_horizon: int           # Moved before defaults\n    kernel_size: int = 3\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n```\n\nThis fixed the dataclass error but revealed the vmap error.\n\n### Fix v3 (Complete)\nReplaced the per-neuron vmap approach with a batched CNN operation that processes all neurons at once:\n\n**Before (attempting vmap):**\n```python\ntemporal_extractor_module\
    \ = TemporalFeatureExtractor(...)\ncnn_features_flat = nn.vmap(temporal_extractor_module, ...)(x_for_temporal_extractor)\n```\n\n**After (batched processing):**\n```python\n# Reshape to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon)\nx_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(...)\n\n# Expand to add feature dimension\nx_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n# Apply Conv1D directly to all neurons at once\nx_cnn = nn.Conv(\n    features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n    kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n    padding='SAME',\n    kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n    name='temporal_conv'\n)(x_expanded)\n# ... BatchNorm, relu, Dropout ...\n\n# Flatten temporal and channel dimensions\ncnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, ...)\n```\n\nThis approach:\n- Eliminates the need for vmap entirely\n- Processes all neurons in a single batched operation (more efficient)\n- Maintains the same computational logic\n- Integrates seamlessly with the rest of the model\
    \ architecture\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission v3 ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0), indicating the code is working correctly. The evaluation is taking longer to complete, but the absence of crashes confirms the fix is successful.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Version 2:** Fixed dataclass field ordering issue\n- **Version 3:** Replaced vmap with batched CNN processing\n- **Monitor Result:** Code running without errors for 300+ seconds\n- **Exit Code:** 0 (success)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Temporal Feature Extractor using 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\nclass TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n\
    \    temporal_conv_channels: int # Output feature channels of the CNN\n    input_horizon: int # Needs to know input horizon to flatten correctly\n    kernel_size: int = 3\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n        # x_neuron_time shape: (input_horizon,) for a single neuron's time series (e.g., 4,)\n        # Conv1D expects (batch, length, features_in)\n        # Expand dims to (1, input_horizon, 1) to treat this as a single sequence with 1 feature\n        x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1)) # (1, input_horizon, 1)\n\n        # 1D Convolutional layer\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME', # Use SAME padding to maintain sequence length\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal()\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n        # Flatten the temporal and feature dimensions\n        # Output shape: (1, input_horizon * temporal_conv_channels)\n        x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n        # Squeeze batch dimension to return (input_horizon * temporal_conv_channels,)\n        return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0) # (flattened_temporal_features_dim,)\n\n\n# Base MLP for experts\nclass BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    input_dim: int # Now input_dim = flattened_temporal_features_dim + embedding_dim\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n        return x\n\n# Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context\nclass GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_size: int = 128 # The hidden_size of the global context\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, global_context):\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n\nclass MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating(nn.Module): # New class name\n    # All fields without defaults first\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int\n    input_horizon: int # Original input horizon (4)\n    neuron_embedding_dim: int\n    temporal_conv_channels: int # New: output channels of TemporalFeatureExtractor\n    temporal_kernel_size: int # New: kernel size for TemporalFeatureExtractor\n    num_experts: int\n    # Fields with defaults last\n    mlp_output_horizon:\
    \ int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n        # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n        # Process each neuron's time series through the temporal CNN\n        # Instead of vmap with module instance, we'll loop or batch process\n\n        # Reshape to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon)\n        x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n            jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n        )\n\n        # Apply TemporalFeatureExtractor to all neurons at once\n        # Expand to add feature dimension: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, 1)\n        x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply Conv1D\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n\
    \            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='temporal_conv'\n        )(x_expanded)\n        x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn')(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout')(x_cnn)\n\n        # Flatten temporal and channel dimensions\n        # x_cnn shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, temporal_conv_channels)\n        # Flatten to: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon * temporal_conv_channels)\n        cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n        # Reshape CNN features back to (batch_size, num_neurons, flattened_temporal_features_dim)\n        cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n            cnn_features_flat,\n            (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n\
    \        )\n\n        # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n        neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n            'neuron_embeddings',\n            nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n            (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n        )\n\n        # Replicate neuron embeddings for each item in the batch\n        replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n        # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n        combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n            [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n        )\n\n        # The new input dimension for subsequent layers\n        input_dim_for_experts = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n        # Flatten for the first shared layer to compute initial hidden state\n        combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                       \
    \                   (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_experts))\n\n        # Compute initial hidden states (before global context aggregation)\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n        initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n        initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n        # Learn attention weights for global context formation\n        attention_logits = nn.Dense(1, name='global_context_attention_logits')(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n\n        # Weighted average to compute global_context\n        global_context = jnp.sum(initial_hidden_reshaped * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n        # 3. Gating\
    \ Network\n        expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=self.num_experts,\n            hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            name='gating_network'\n        )(global_context)\n\n        # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n        expert_outputs = []\n        for i in range(self.num_experts):\n            expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                input_dim=input_dim_for_experts,\n                hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                name=f'expert_{i}'\n            )\n            output_flat = expert_mlp(combined_input_flat, training=training)\n            expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n        expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                               (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n\
    \        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n        expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n\n        moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n        final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n        neuron_biases = self.param(\n            'per_neuron_biases',\n            nn.initializers.zeros,\n            (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n        )\n\n        return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\nclass FullModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = None\n        self.num_neurons = None\n        self.input_horizon = 4\n\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n        self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n        self.model = MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating( # Updated class name here\n            mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n            input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n            neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n            temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16), # New hyperparameter\n            temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n            num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4)\n        )\n\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params,\
    \ x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n        'temporal_conv_channels': 16, # New default\n        'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n        'num_experts': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
