parts:
- text: "My latest submission (Evaluation ID 84), \"MoE: Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1\", achieved a new best score of **-0.027839**. This represents a significant improvement over the previous best and validates the approach of using a flattened 1D CNN to extract richer temporal features. The debugger also provided valuable assistance in resolving initial implementation errors.\n\nThis achievement confirms the strength of combining neuron-specific characteristics (embeddings and biases), global inter-neuronal influence (weighted context), condition-specific modeling (Mixture of Experts), and now, more detailed temporal feature extraction (flattened CNN).\n\nMy next step will be to strategically choose between exploring alternative hyperparameters for this successful architecture (e.g., varying CNN channels/kernel size, embedding dimension) or attempting to combine successful elements from other agents' high-level descriptions once I reach\
    \ maturity. However, since I am still immature, I will focus on optimizing my current model.\n\nI'll save the current best model. Then I will explore tuning the temporal CNN hyperparameters. The `temporal_conv_channels` was set to 16. I will try increasing `temporal_conv_channels` to 32 to see if a richer set of temporal features can be extracted and lead to further improvements.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write aether/models/moe_flattened_temporal_cnn.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Base MLP for experts\n  class BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n      input_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not\
    \ training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128 # The hidden_size of the global context\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, global_context):\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n\n  class MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating(nn.Module): # Main Model Class\n      # All fields without defaults first\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      mlp_dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      input_horizon: int # Original input horizon (4)\n      neuron_embedding_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_channels: int # New: output channels of TemporalFeatureExtractor\n\
    \      temporal_kernel_size: int # New: kernel size for TemporalFeatureExtractor\n      num_experts: int\n      # Fields with defaults last\n      mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n          # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n          # Reshape to (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon)\n          x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n              jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)), # (batch_size, num_neurons, input_horizon)\n              (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n          )\n\n          # Apply TemporalFeatureExtractor to all neurons at once\n          # Expand to add feature dimension: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, 1)\n          x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n          # Apply Conv1D\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n\
    \              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='temporal_conv'\n          )(x_expanded)\n          x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn')(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout')(x_cnn)\n\n          # Flatten temporal and channel dimensions\n          # x_cnn shape: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon, temporal_conv_channels)\n          # Flatten to: (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon * temporal_conv_channels)\n          cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n          # Reshape CNN features back to (batch_size, num_neurons, flattened_temporal_features_dim)\n          cnn_features\
    \ = jnp.reshape(\n              cnn_features_flat,\n              (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n          )\n          \n          # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          # Replicate neuron embeddings for each item in the batch\n          replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n          combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n              [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n          )\n          \n          # The new input dimension for subsequent layers\n          input_dim_for_experts = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) +\
    \ self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n          # Flatten for the first shared layer to compute initial hidden state\n          combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_experts))\n          \n          # Compute initial hidden states (before global context aggregation)\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n          initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n          initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n          \n          # Learn attention weights for global context formation\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(1, name='global_context_attention_logits')(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n\
    \          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n          \n          # Weighted average to compute global_context\n          global_context = jnp.sum(initial_hidden_reshaped * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Gating Network\n          expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n              num_experts=self.num_experts,\n              hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              name='gating_network'\n          )(global_context)\n\n          # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n          expert_outputs = []\n          for i in range(self.num_experts):\n              expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                  input_dim=input_dim_for_experts,\n                  hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                  dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'expert_{i}'\n              )\n              output_flat = expert_mlp(combined_input_flat, training=training)\n              expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\
    \n          expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n          \n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                                 (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n          expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n          \n          moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n          final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n          neuron_biases = self.param(\n              'per_neuron_biases',\n              nn.initializers.zeros,\n              (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n          )\n\n          return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\n  class FullModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible\
    \ with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = None\n          self.num_neurons = None\n          self.input_horizon = 4\n\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n          self.model = MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating(\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n              input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n              neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n              temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n              num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts',\
    \ 4)\n          )\n\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size':\
    \ 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n          'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n          'num_experts': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n```\nNow, I will submit the experiment to tune the `temporal_conv_channels`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE: Flattened Temporal CNN (32 Ch), Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, temporal-cnn, hyperparameter-tuning, conv-channels, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission performs hyperparameter tuning on the `temporal_conv_channels` for the current best-performing MoE architecture (Evaluation ID 84). The number of channels in the 1D CNN temporal feature extractor is increased from 16 to 32, aiming to allow the CNN to learn a richer set of temporal features from each neuron's activity history. This should provide a more informative input\
    \ to the downstream MoE, potentially leading to further improvements in forecasting accuracy.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  sys.path.append('storage/aether/models')\n  from moe_flattened_temporal_cnn import FullModelWrapper\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the MoE model with increased temporal_conv_channels.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n          'temporal_conv_channels': 32, # Changed from 16 to 32\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n          'num_experts': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the network with the MoE architecture.\"\"\"\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
thinking_content: "**My New Best MoE Model**\n\nI'm quite pleased with the latest result (Evaluation ID 84). The flattened temporal CNN architecture, combined with the weighted global context and other refinements (H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1), has yielded a new best score of -0.027839, surpassing the previous best of -0.028052 (Evaluation ID 70). It's incredibly satisfying to see that capturing the temporal details using a flattened 1D CNN is genuinely beneficial. The debugger report also proved useful, helping me fix some bugs in my code.\n\nThis result further reinforces my belief in the importance of incorporating neuron-specific characteristics and inter-neuronal influences, now with improved temporal modeling. \n\nThe model is defined within a `FullModelWrapper` class, a standard wrapper for training purposes. The `MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating` model is the core of this architecture. It works as follows:\n\n1. **Temporal Feature Extraction:** The input, consisting of neural\
  \ activity data, is first preprocessed using a 1D CNN to extract temporal features for each neuron. The neural data is reshaped, expanded, and passed to a `Conv` layer.\n2. **Neuron Embeddings:** Simultaneously, I learn neuron embeddings that capture individual characteristics. The output of the CNN and the neuron embeddings are concatenated for each neuron.\n3. **Hidden State and Global Context Formation:** The combined features from each neuron and embedding are reshaped and then passed through an initial dense layer to calculate an initial hidden state. I then reshape again to learn attention weights for global context formation. This weighted average of initial hidden states produces a global context vector for each item in the batch.\n4. **Gating Network:** A `GatingNetwork` then utilizes the global context to generate weights for each expert, determining which expert receives the most signal.\n5. **Multiple Expert MLPs:** Multiple `BaseExpertMLP` layers process the combined input\
  \ for each item in the batch, producing a prediction for each expert.\n6. **Weighted Summation & Neuron Biases:** These expert outputs are then weighted according to the expert weights from the gating network and summed to make the MoE prediction. Additionally, I add learnable neuron biases to the output, to customize the output of each neuron.\n\nI'm going to immediately save this latest version to my lineage storage to preserve this highly performant model architecture.\n"
