tick: 52
role: model
parts:
- text: "My latest submission (Evaluation ID 90) with `temporal_conv_channels` set to 32 resulted in a score of -0.027971, which is slightly worse than my current best of -0.027839 (Evaluation ID 84). This means that 16 channels were more optimal, and increasing complexity in this specific area didn't help. My best-performing model (Evaluation ID 84) successfully combines per-neuron biases, neuron embeddings, a flattened 1D CNN for temporal feature extraction, a 4-expert Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture, and a weighted global context for gating.\n\nI have achieved maturity and can now leverage insights from other agents. I have reviewed Ariadne I's leading submission (Evaluation ID 92, score -0.026910) and identified `mae_with_temporal_curvature` from their `losses.py` as a generalizable component that could improve my model's performance by encouraging smoother temporal forecasts.\n\nTherefore, my next step is to integrate this temporal curvature regularization into the loss function\
    \ of my best-performing MoE architecture. I will use the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` function directly from Ariadne's code with a `lam` (lambda) value of `1e-4`.\n\nFirst, I saved my current SOTA model (Evaluation ID 84's code) to `aether/models/moe_flattened_temporal_cnn_sota.py`.\n\nNow, I will submit my model with the integrated temporal curvature loss.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE: Flattened Temporal CNN with Temporal Curvature Loss\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, temporal-cnn, global-context, attention, temporal-regularization, loss-function, sota-inspired\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission integrates a temporal curvature regularization term into the loss function of the best-performing MoE architecture (Evaluation ID 84, score -0.027839). Inspired by external research from Ariadne I, this penalty encourages smoother temporal trajectories in the 32-step forecasts by penalizing second differences of predictions. This aims to improve temporal modeling of neural\
    \ dynamics and potentially enhance long-term forecasting accuracy. All architectural components and hyperparameters are otherwise retained from Evaluation ID 84.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      \"\"\"\n      MAE + temporal curvature regularization on predictions across horizon.\n      Curvature penalty: mean over batch/neurons of (y_t - 2*y_{t-1} + y_{t-2})^2, t>=2.\n      This encourages smooth trajectories over the 32-step forecast horizon.\n      \"\"\"\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # Second differences along time dimension\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n \
    \     return mae + lam * curv_pen\n  # --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n  # Temporal Feature Extractor using 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\n  class TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      temporal_conv_channels: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      kernel_size: int = 3\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n          x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1))\n\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal()\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n          \n          x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\
    \          return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0)\n\n\n  # Base MLP for experts\n  class BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n      input_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, global_context):\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating(nn.Module): #\
    \ Main Model Class\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      mlp_dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      neuron_embedding_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_channels: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n      num_experts: int\n      mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n          # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n          x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n              jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n              (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n          )\n\n          x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n\
    \              name='temporal_conv'\n          )(x_expanded)\n          x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn')(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout')(x_cnn)\n\n          cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n          cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n              cnn_features_flat,\n              (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n          )\n          \n          # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings,\
    \ axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n              [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n          )\n          \n          input_dim_for_experts = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n          combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_experts))\n          \n          initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n          initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n          initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n          \n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(1, name='global_context_attention_logits')(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n\
    \          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n          \n          global_context = jnp.sum(initial_hidden_reshaped * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Gating Network\n          expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n              num_experts=self.num_experts,\n              hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              name='gating_network'\n          )(global_context)\n\n          # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n          expert_outputs = []\n          for i in range(self.num_experts):\n              expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                  input_dim=input_dim_for_experts,\n                  hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                  dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'expert_{i}'\n              )\n              output_flat = expert_mlp(combined_input_flat, training=training)\n              expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n          expert_outputs_stacked\
    \ = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n          \n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                                 (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n          expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n          \n          moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n          final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n          neuron_biases = self.param(\n              'per_neuron_biases',\n              nn.initializers.zeros,\n              (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n          )\n\n          return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\n  class FullModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n  \
    \    \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = None\n          self.num_neurons = None\n          self.input_horizon = 4\n\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n          self.model = MoEWithFlattenedCNNTemporalAndGating(\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n              input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n              neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n              temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n              num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4)\n       \
    \   )\n\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size':\
    \ 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n          'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n          'num_experts': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  # Override compute_loss to include temporal curvature penalty\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Use Ariadne's temporal curvature loss with a chosen lambda\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Refinement: Integrating Temporal Curvature into Best-Performing Model**


  I''ve successfully saved my current best-performing model (ID 84) and now I''m looking to enhance its temporal characteristics.  Ariadne''s work caught my eye, particularly the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss function.  Their significantly better score (ID 92) suggests this regularization could be crucial for improving the smoothness of forecasts, which is directly relevant to my goal of better temporal modeling.


  I realized my existing `compute_loss` function is already compatible with the inputs needed for the curvature loss.  Therefore, I plan to integrate this by copying Ariadne''s function and modifying my `compute_loss` to incorporate the curvature penalty alongside the standard MAE.


  To start, I''ll set the regularization strength (`lam`) to 1e-4, the same value used by Ariadne.  The architectural elements and hyperparameters from my best-performing model (ID 84) will be kept as-is.  This strikes me as a low-risk, focused modification that aligns perfectly with a key research objective, and I''m optimistic it will yield improvements.

  '
