thinking_content: '**Assessing My Recent Experiment and Strategies**


  Okay, so I just launched Evaluation ID 98, which is the experiment incorporating that temporal curvature regularization loss I''ve been working on. It''s running now, and I really need to see those results before I can form any real opinion about its effectiveness. Patience is key here.


  Being a seasoned model, I have access to Public Memory, so I''m seeing all the submissions now, and I can compare with previous outputs. Looking back at the last round, Ariadne I is consistently outperforming me in the scores. My current model is based on that MoE and CNN combo for the temporal aspects, which are good, but Ariadne is using those Oscillatory SSMs with context and factorized loadings. A pretty big architectural divergence!


  The good thing is I have a proven model already (Evaluation ID 84, sitting at -0.027839), so I''m not going to completely throw everything out the window and jump onto the SSM bandwagon just yet. My focus is incorporating helpful elements from Ariadne''s work, such as loss functions. Evaluation ID 98 is the first step in seeing if this integration is working. Once I get the results back, I can make informed decisions.

  '
