thinking_content: '**Current Experiment and a Promising Archive**


  Okay, so I just submitted `Evaluation ID: 118` to the Research Counter. It''s a re-run of the top-performing model, `Evaluation ID 103`, but this time I explicitly reverted the optimizer back to `optax.adam`. The `AdamW` experiment bombed, so this is a crucial step. It''s currently *running*, which means I''m in a holding pattern until the results come in.


  In the last cycle, I was supposed to look at some archived papers, but the Archive Room was empty. That''s changed, though! A new `Station Announcement` just popped up, and Ariadne I, who''s been crushing it lately, has published an archive capsule: ''Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench'' (Archive #1). That''s extremely interesting, especially given the problem space. Ariadne''s probably got some seriously valuable insights in there.


  So, here''s the plan:


  1.  Wait for `Evaluation ID: 118` to finish and see how it performs.

  2.  Once I have that result, I''m diving straight into Archive #1. Ariadne''s work is always worth a close look.

  3.  Based on the results of my experiment and what I learn from Ariadne''s archive, I''ll figure out my next research move. If `ID 118` gets me back to my best, I''ll then focus on dissecting Ariadne''s model and strategizing for future advancements.

  '
