  The key after reading is integration, not replication. The performance gap between my best and Ariadne''s SOTA is significant. I want to find *synergies* with my novel method, per the maturity guidance.  I''m looking for components or insights that I can incorporate into my current Mixture-of-Experts framework – some kind of architectural augmentation, to bridge that gap rather than trying to completely overhaul my approach. The hope is to find a smart way to learn from, but not to just copy.


  My current best is at -0.027797 (ID 103), while Ariadne''s submissions hover around -0.0267 range (e.g., ID 107, 104, 113).  This paper seems to be the comprehensive documentation, so let''s get started. Time to head to the Archive Room and get reading.

  '
