tick: 70
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 70\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 359,356 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoE: Factorized MLP Experts, Spatial CNN (Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss' (ID: 126) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028318028348130565\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0265\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0294\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0314\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 126\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Python dataclass field ordering error in Flax module definition.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe\
    \ original code had a `TypeError` in the `FactorizedExpertMLP` class definition at line 41:\n\n```\nTypeError: non-default argument 'num_neurons' follows default argument\n```\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax modules use internally), all fields with default values must come **after** all fields without default values. The original class had:\n\n```python\nclass FactorizedExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    mlp_hidden_size: int              # No default\n    output_horizon: int = 32          # Has default\n    factor_rank_p: int = 32           # Has default\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1         # Has default\n    num_neurons: int                  # No default - ERROR!\n```\n\nThe field `num_neurons` (without a default) came after fields with defaults, violating Python's dataclass rules.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 2**: Reordered the class fields to place all non-default parameters before default parameters:\n\n```python\nclass FactorizedExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    mlp_hidden_size: int   \
    \           # No default\n    num_neurons: int                  # No default (moved up)\n    output_horizon: int = 32          # Has default\n    factor_rank_p: int = 32           # Has default\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1         # Has default\n```\n\nAlso updated the corresponding instantiation in the main model to match the new parameter order:\n\n```python\nexpert_mlp = FactorizedExpertMLP(\n    mlp_hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n    num_neurons=self.num_neurons,     # Updated order\n    output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n    factor_rank_p=self.factor_rank_p,\n    dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n    name=f'expert_{i}'\n)\n```\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs without crashing. The evaluation has been running for over 300 seconds, indicating the fix was successful. The submission can now proceed with training the Mixture of Experts model with factorized MLP experts, spatial CNN hidden layers, and temporal curvature loss.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot\
    \ modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n# --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n# Temporal Feature Extractor using a 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\nclass TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    temporal_conv_channels: int\n    input_horizon: int\n    kernel_size: int = 3\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n        x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1))\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='temporal_conv_1'\n        )(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x)\n\n        x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n        return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0)\n\n# Factorized MLP Expert (replaces BaseExpertMLP)\nclass FactorizedExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    mlp_hidden_size: int # Input hidden dimension (from previous layer)\n    num_neurons: int # To define U matrix (moved before default parameters)\n    output_horizon: int =\
    \ 32\n    factor_rank_p: int = 32 # New: Factorization rank\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, features_for_expert, training: bool = False):\n        # features_for_expert shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n        batch_size, num_neurons, _ = features_for_expert.shape\n\n        # First layer of factorization: U matrix (num_neurons x factor_rank_p)\n        # U matrix takes features (mlp_hidden_size) and maps them to factor space (factor_rank_p)\n        # We define U as a dense layer applied to the features.\n        # Input (batch, neurons, hidden_size) -> Output (batch, neurons, factor_rank_p)\n        factor_space_features = nn.Dense(\n            features=self.factor_rank_p,\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='U_factor_projection'\n        )(features_for_expert) # (batch, num_neurons, factor_rank_p)\n\n        # LayerNorm or BatchNorm in factor space for stability, as suggested by Ariadne\n\
    \        factor_space_features = nn.LayerNorm(name='factor_layernorm')(factor_space_features)\n        factor_space_features = nn.relu(factor_space_features)\n        factor_space_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(factor_space_features)\n\n        # Second layer of factorization: V matrix (factor_rank_p x output_horizon)\n        # This is applied to the factor space features to project to the output horizon\n        # It needs to be shared across neurons, and operate on each factor independently.\n        # The simplest interpretation for a shared V is another Dense layer\n        # (batch, num_neurons, factor_rank_p) -> (batch, num_neurons, output_horizon)\n        predictions_unflat = nn.Dense(\n            features=self.output_horizon,\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='V_output_projection'\n        )(factor_space_features) # (batch, num_neurons, output_horizon)\n\n        # The output from FactorizedExpertMLP\
    \ should be (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon)\n        # to be consistent with how the MoE blends them.\n        return jnp.reshape(predictions_unflat, (batch_size * num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n\n# Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context\nclass GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, global_context):\n        logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass MoEWithFactorizedExpertsAndGating(nn.Module): # New class name\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int\n    input_horizon: int\n    neuron_embedding_dim: int\n    temporal_conv_channels: int\n    temporal_kernel_size: int\n    spatial_kernel_size: int\n    factor_rank_p: int # New: Factorization rank for experts\n    num_experts: int\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neural_activity,\
    \ training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n        # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n        x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n            jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n        )\n\n        x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='temporal_conv_1'\n        )(x_expanded)\n        x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x_cnn)\n\n        cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn,\
    \ (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n        cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n            cnn_features_flat,\n            (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n        )\n\n        # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n        neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n            'neuron_embeddings',\n            nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n            (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n        )\n\n        replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n        # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n        combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n            [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n        )\n\n        input_dim_for_initial_dense = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n        combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n\
    \                                            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_initial_dense))\n\n        # Compute initial hidden states\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n        initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n        initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n        # Spatial CNN Layer on Hidden States\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            kernel_size=(self.spatial_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='spatial_cnn_on_hidden_layer'\n        )(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not\
    \ training, name='spatial_bn')(spatial_output_hidden)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.relu(spatial_output_hidden)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='spatial_dropout')(spatial_output_hidden)\n\n        features_for_gating_and_experts = spatial_output_hidden # (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n\n        # Learn attention weights for global context formation\n        attention_logits = nn.Dense(1, name='global_context_attention_logits')(features_for_gating_and_experts)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n\n        global_context = jnp.sum(features_for_gating_and_experts * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n        # 3. Gating Network\n        expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=self.num_experts,\n            hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            name='gating_network'\n        )(global_context)\n\n        # 4. Multiple Factorized Expert MLPs\n     \
    \   expert_outputs = []\n        for i in range(self.num_experts):\n            expert_mlp = FactorizedExpertMLP( # Using FactorizedExpertMLP\n                mlp_hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n                output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                factor_rank_p=self.factor_rank_p,\n                dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                name=f'expert_{i}'\n            )\n            # Pass features_for_gating_and_experts as input to the factorized expert\n            output_flat = expert_mlp(features_for_gating_and_experts, training=training) # (batch_size * num_neurons, output_horizon)\n            expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n        expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                         (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n        expert_outputs_for_blend\
    \ = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n        expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n\n        moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n        final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n        neuron_biases = self.param(\n            'per_neuron_biases',\n            nn.initializers.zeros,\n            (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n        )\n\n        return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\nclass FullModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = None\n        self.num_neurons = None\n        self.input_horizon = 4\n\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n       \
    \ self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n        self.model = MoEWithFactorizedExpertsAndGating( # Updated class name here\n            mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n            input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n            neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n            temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n            temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n            spatial_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('spatial_kernel_size', 3),\n            factor_rank_p=self.hparams.get('factor_rank_p', 32), # New hyperparameter\n            num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4)\n        )\n\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n        \
    \    dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n        'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n        'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n        'spatial_kernel_size': 3,\n        'factor_rank_p': 32, # New default\n \
    \       'num_experts': 4\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.232026\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training\
    \ run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 220876 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 220879\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate':\
