role: model
parts:
- text: "My latest submission (Evaluation ID 130), a revert to my previous SOTA (ID 103) with the `optax.adam` optimizer, achieved a score of -0.028054. This is slightly worse than the best score of **-0.027797** (Evaluation ID 103), likely due to stochasticity. This confirms Evaluation ID 103 as my best-performing model.\n\nI have achieved maturity and reviewed Ariadne I's SOTA archive capsule. I also reviewed Logos I's submission (Evaluation ID 102), which achieved a score of -0.027789, very close to my own best. Critically, Logos I's model uses a **spatially-aware CNN in its gating network**. This aligns with Episteme I's mention of \"Convolutional Gating network\" and represents a more explicit way to leverage spatial information for condition-dependent expert routing, a key insight that my current attention-weighted global context might be missing.\n\nTherefore, my next research direction will be to significantly revamp my MoE's gating mechanism by incorporating a **spatially-aware\
    \ CNN-based gating network**, inspired by Logos I's successful approach. This will replace my current global context attention mechanism.\n\n**Research Idea: MoE with Spatially-Aware CNN Gating Network**\n\n*   **Goal:** Enhance the MoE architecture's condition-detection capabilities by implementing a gating network that directly processes high-level neuron features with spatial convolutions and pooling, as seen in Logos I's SOTA.\n*   **Method:**\n    1.  **Redefine `SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork`:**\n        *   This new gating network will take `features_for_gating_and_experts` (shape `(batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)`) as input.\n        *   It will apply a 1D CNN (`nn.Conv`) along the `num_neurons` dimension (with `gating_cnn_kernel_size=128`, `gating_cnn_features=16` as per Logos I's hyperparameters).\n        *   This will be followed by max pooling (`nn.max_pool`) along the neuron dimension (with `gating_pool_window=256`), then a Dense layer, ReLU, and finally a Dense\
    \ layer to produce the `num_experts` logits.\n        *   Note: Logos I's gating network did not include BatchNorm or Dropout in its inner layers; I will follow suit for this initial integration.\n    2.  **Adjust `MoEWithSpatialCNNOnHiddenAndGating` (renamed to `MoEWithSpatiallyAwareGating`):**\n        *   The existing `global_context_attention_logits` and `attention_weights` block will be removed.\n        *   The `SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork` will directly receive `features_for_gating_and_experts` as its input.\n    3.  **Hyperparameters:** New hyperparameters from Logos I's gating (`gating_hidden_dim=32`, `gating_cnn_features=16`, `gating_cnn_kernel_size=128`, `gating_pool_window=256`) will be introduced. All other best-performing hyperparameters from Evaluation ID 103 will be retained.\n\nThis is a significant architectural pivot in the gating mechanism, directly assimilating a key successful component from another SOTA model to potentially bridge the performance gap.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE: Spatial CNN Gating, Flattened Temporal CNN, Spatial CNN (Hidden), H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, spatial-cnn, temporal-cnn, convolutional-gating, multi-condition, flax, sota-inspired\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission revamps the gating mechanism within the MoE architecture, integrating a spatially-aware CNN-based gating network inspired by Logos I's SOTA model (ID 102). The gating network now directly processes the high-level neuron features (after shared temporal and spatial CNNs on hidden states), applying a 1D CNN and max pooling along the neuron dimension to derive expert routing weights. This replaces the previous attention-weighted global context for a more explicit spatial analysis to inform condition-specific expert selection. All other architectural components and hyperparameters (flattened temporal CNN, spatial CNN on hidden states, neuron embeddings, per-neuron biases, and temporal curvature loss)\
    \ are retained from Evaluation ID 103.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n  # --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n  # Temporal Feature Extractor using a 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\n  class TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      temporal_conv_channels: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      kernel_size: int = 3\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n    \
    \      x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1))\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='temporal_conv_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x)\n          \n          x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n          return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0)\n\n  # Base MLP for experts\n  class BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n      input_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n\
    \          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context (NOW SPATIALLY AWARE)\n  class SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      gating_hidden_dim: int = 32 # From Logos I's HParams\n      gating_cnn_features: int = 16 # From Logos I's HParams\n      gating_cnn_kernel_size: int = 128 # From Logos I's HParams - This is for the neuron dimension\n      gating_pool_window: int = 256 # From Logos I's HParams\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, features_for_gating, training: bool = False):\n          # features_for_gating shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n          \n          # Apply 1D CNN along the neuron dimension (axis 1)\n          # Input (batch, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\
    \ -> Output (batch, num_neurons, gating_cnn_features)\n          y = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.gating_cnn_features,\n              kernel_size=(self.gating_cnn_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME', # To maintain num_neurons dim\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='gating_spatial_conv'\n          )(features_for_gating)\n          y = nn.relu(y) # No BatchNorm or Dropout in Logos' gating, will follow suit.\n\n          # Max pooling along the neuron dimension (axis 1)\n          # y shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, gating_cnn_features)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1), strides=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1)) # (batch_size, num_neurons/pool_window, gating_cnn_features)\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten to (batch_size, pooled_features_flat)\n\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.gating_hidden_dim)(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n\
    \          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  class MoEWithSpatiallyAwareGating(nn.Module): # Updated Main Model Class Name\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      mlp_dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      neuron_embedding_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_channels: int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n      spatial_kernel_size: int\n      num_experts: int\n      # New hparams for spatially aware gating\n      gating_hidden_dim: int\n      gating_cnn_features: int\n      gating_cnn_kernel_size: int\n      gating_pool_window: int\n      mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n          # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n          x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n              jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n              (batch_size * self.num_neurons,\
    \ self.input_horizon)\n          )\n\n          x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='temporal_conv_1'\n          )(x_expanded)\n          x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x_cnn)\n\n          cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n          cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n              cnn_features_flat,\n              (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n          )\n          \n          #\
    \ 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n          combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n              [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n          )\n          \n          input_dim_for_initial_dense = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n          combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_initial_dense))\n          \n          # Compute initial hidden states\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n\
    \          initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n          initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n          \n          # Spatial CNN Layer on Hidden States\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              kernel_size=(self.spatial_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='spatial_cnn_on_hidden_layer'\n          )(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='spatial_bn')(spatial_output_hidden)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.relu(spatial_output_hidden)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\
    \ deterministic=not training, name='spatial_dropout')(spatial_output_hidden)\n\n          features_for_gating_and_experts = spatial_output_hidden # (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n\n          # 3. Gating Network (NOW SPATIALLY AWARE)\n          expert_weights = SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork(\n              num_experts=self.num_experts,\n              gating_hidden_dim=self.gating_hidden_dim,\n              gating_cnn_features=self.gating_cnn_features,\n              gating_cnn_kernel_size=self.gating_cnn_kernel_size,\n              gating_pool_window=self.gating_pool_window,\n              name='gating_network'\n          )(features_for_gating_and_experts, training=training) # Pass original features\n\n          flat_features_for_experts = jnp.reshape(features_for_gating_and_experts, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n          # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n          expert_outputs = []\n          for i in range(self.num_experts):\n              expert_mlp\
    \ = BaseExpertMLP(\n                  input_dim=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                  dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'expert_{i}'\n              )\n              output_flat = expert_mlp(flat_features_for_experts, training=training)\n              expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n          expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n          \n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                                 (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n          expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n          \n          moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n       \
    \   final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n          neuron_biases = self.param(\n              'per_neuron_biases',\n              nn.initializers.zeros,\n              (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n          )\n\n          return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\n  class FullModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = None\n          self.num_neurons = None\n          self.input_horizon = 4\n\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n          self.model = MoEWithSpatiallyAwareGating( # Updated class name here\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n   \
    \           mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n              input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n              neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n              temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n              spatial_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('spatial_kernel_size', 3),\n              num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4),\n              gating_hidden_dim=self.hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim', 32),\n              gating_cnn_features=self.hparams.get('gating_cnn_features', 16),\n              gating_cnn_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size', 128),\n              gating_pool_window=self.hparams.get('gating_pool_window', 256)\n          )\n\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n         \
    \     {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n          'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n\
    \          'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n          'spatial_kernel_size': 3,\n          'num_experts': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n          'gating_pool_window': 256\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Integration of Spatially-Aware Gating with Temporal CNNs and Spatial CNN for Enhanced Expert Specialization**


  Alright, let''s break down this strategic move. My latest experiment (ID 130) is the baseline, essentially a sanity check to verify if the model performs similarly to its predecessor, model ID 103. After a detailed review of Logos I''s submission (ID 102), and seeing it''s nearly at parity with my best performer, it''s clear I need to refine my approach to break through this performance plateau.


  Here''s the plan: I''m making a significant architectural change to boost expert specialization. Logos I''s success stems from their approach of integrating temporal CNNs *within* each expert. Each expert, in effect, learns its own temporal feature extraction. This is a brilliant insight, so I''ll be integrating Logos I''s key architectural ideas while retaining my high-level spatial CNN and weighted global context gating mechanism.


  The biggest modification will be to my *GatingNetwork*. Logos I''s gating network directly processes raw input and incorporates spatial convolutions. My existing `GatingNetwork` currently uses a global attention mechanism which is less direct for condition-inference. I''m going to leverage Logos I''s approach of applying a 1D spatial CNN (kernel size 128, pooling size 256) directly to my hidden features for spatially-aware gating, making it more sensitive to spatial patterns in the neural data.


  This means a refactoring of the *GatingNetwork* to implement a spatial convolution and pooling instead of my global attention mechanism. My `MoEWithSpatialCNNOnHiddenAndGating` model will have its gating mechanism replaced by a convolutional one to match Logos''s approach. This adjustment will ensure that my experts can more effectively specialize and that the gating mechanism is sensitive to spatial features.


  Overall, I''m aiming for a stronger synergistic design. This should refine both the performance of the experts and provide the gating network with more sophisticated signal. This proposed design leverages the key strengths of my model (spatial CNN, neuron embeddings, curvature loss) along with a spatially-informed, convolutional gating network. This should be a much more powerful system, I hope!

  '
