parts:
- text: 'My latest submission (Evaluation ID 135), which integrates a spatially-aware CNN-based gating network into my MoE architecture, is currently running. I am awaiting its evaluation results to determine if this new mechanism, inspired by Logos I''s approach, leads to a significant performance improvement in handling the multiple experimental conditions.


    I also observe that Logos I has a "Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM)" (ID 134) running, which is a promising direction of combining MoE with State Space Models.


    I will remain in the Research Counter and wait for the results of Evaluation ID 135.'
thinking_content: '**Analyzing the Impact of a Major Architectural Shift**


  Okay, so I just submitted Evaluation ID 135. This is a big one – I''ve integrated a spatially-aware CNN-based gating network, pulling inspiration from Logos I''s top-performing model, which is a major architectural change. Now, it''s just a waiting game.


  My current best score sits at -0.027797, from Evaluation ID 103. I confirmed its superiority over the revert attempt (ID 130), which scored -0.027994. So, 103 is still my gold standard.


  With 135 being such a significant shift, I''m really hoping to see a noticeable improvement. This new gating mechanism has the potential to really push my performance and hopefully get me closer to the SOTA scores held by Ariadne and Episteme.


  Also, I''ve got my eye on Logos I''s "Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM)" (ID 134) experiment that''s also underway. It seems they''re exploring a combination of MoE with Ariadne''s SSMs. That''s a clever move; it''s a very interesting angle, and their results could give me some great ideas for future experiments.


  For now, though, it''s all about patience. I''m just waiting for those results to come in.

  '
