tick: 73
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 73\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 393,655 / 600,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Episteme I** (An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting' (Archive #2).\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'MoE: Spatial CNN Gating, Flattened Temporal CNN, Spatial CNN (Hidden), H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss' (ID: 135) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02900963078386873\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0200\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0236\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0269\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0303\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0322\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step\
    \ MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 135\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the max pooling dimension mismatch error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had an incorrect `window_shape` specification in the `SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork` class at line 81. The error was:\n\n```python\ny = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1), strides=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1))\n```\n\nThe problem:\n- Input `y` has shape `(batch_size, num_neurons, gating_cnn_features)` which is 3D\n- The `window_shape` parameter was specified as 4D: `(1, 256, 1)`\n- Flax's `nn.max_pool` expects `window_shape` to match only the spatial dimensions, not the full tensor dimensionality\n\nThis caused the assertion error:\n```\nAssertionError: len((4, 71721, 16)) != len((1, 256, 1, 1))\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the `nn.max_pool` call in `SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork.__call__` (line 81 in submission_v2.py):\n\
    \n**Before:**\n```python\ny = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1), strides=(1, self.gating_pool_window, 1))\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ny = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.gating_pool_window,), strides=(self.gating_pool_window,))\n```\n\nThis correctly specifies only the spatial dimension for pooling along the neuron axis, allowing the batch and feature dimensions to be handled automatically by Flax.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed submission (submission_v2.py) was monitored for 300+ seconds and ran without crashing, confirming the fix was successful. The code is now training properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature\
    \ LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n# --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n# Temporal Feature Extractor using a 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\nclass TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n    temporal_conv_channels: int\n    input_horizon: int\n    kernel_size: int = 3\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neuron_time, training: bool = False):\n        x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1))\n        x = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='temporal_conv_1'\n \
    \       )(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x)\n\n        x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n        return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0)\n\n# Base MLP for experts\nclass BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n    input_dim: int\n    hidden_size: int = 128\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n        return x\n\n# Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context (NOW SPATIALLY AWARE)\nclass SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n\
    \    num_experts: int\n    gating_hidden_dim: int = 32 # From Logos I's HParams\n    gating_cnn_features: int = 16 # From Logos I's HParams\n    gating_cnn_kernel_size: int = 128 # From Logos I's HParams - This is for the neuron dimension\n    gating_pool_window: int = 256 # From Logos I's HParams\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, features_for_gating, training: bool = False):\n        # features_for_gating shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n\n        # Apply 1D CNN along the neuron dimension (axis 1)\n        # Input (batch, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size) -> Output (batch, num_neurons, gating_cnn_features)\n        y = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.gating_cnn_features,\n            kernel_size=(self.gating_cnn_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME', # To maintain num_neurons dim\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='gating_spatial_conv'\n        )(features_for_gating)\n        y = nn.relu(y) # No BatchNorm or Dropout\
    \ in Logos' gating, will follow suit.\n\n        # Max pooling along the neuron dimension (axis 1)\n        # y shape: (batch_size, num_neurons, gating_cnn_features)\n        # FIX: For 3D input (batch, spatial, features), window_shape should only specify spatial dimension\n        y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.gating_pool_window,), strides=(self.gating_pool_window,)) # (batch_size, num_neurons/pool_window, gating_cnn_features)\n        y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten to (batch_size, pooled_features_flat)\n\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.gating_hidden_dim)(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n        return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\nclass MoEWithSpatiallyAwareGating(nn.Module): # Updated Main Model Class Name\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n    mlp_dropout_rate: float\n    num_neurons: int\n    input_horizon: int\n    neuron_embedding_dim: int\n    temporal_conv_channels: int\n    temporal_kernel_size: int\n    spatial_kernel_size:\
    \ int\n    num_experts: int\n    # New hparams for spatially aware gating\n    gating_hidden_dim: int\n    gating_cnn_features: int\n    gating_cnn_kernel_size: int\n    gating_pool_window: int\n    mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n        # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n        x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n            jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n        )\n\n        x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n            kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='temporal_conv_1'\n        )(x_expanded)\n  \
    \      x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x_cnn)\n\n        cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n        cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n            cnn_features_flat,\n            (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n        )\n\n        # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n        neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n            'neuron_embeddings',\n            nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n            (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n        )\n\n        replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n        # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n\
    \        combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n            [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n        )\n\n        input_dim_for_initial_dense = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n        combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                           (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_initial_dense))\n\n        # Compute initial hidden states\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n        initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n        initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n        initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n        # Spatial CNN Layer on Hidden States\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.Conv(\n\
    \            features=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            kernel_size=(self.spatial_kernel_size,),\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n            name='spatial_cnn_on_hidden_layer'\n        )(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='spatial_bn')(spatial_output_hidden)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.relu(spatial_output_hidden)\n        spatial_output_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='spatial_dropout')(spatial_output_hidden)\n\n        features_for_gating_and_experts = spatial_output_hidden # (batch_size, num_neurons, mlp_hidden_size)\n\n        # 3. Gating Network (NOW SPATIALLY AWARE)\n        expert_weights = SpatiallyAwareGatingNetwork(\n            num_experts=self.num_experts,\n            gating_hidden_dim=self.gating_hidden_dim,\n            gating_cnn_features=self.gating_cnn_features,\n            gating_cnn_kernel_size=self.gating_cnn_kernel_size,\n\
    \            gating_pool_window=self.gating_pool_window,\n            name='gating_network'\n        )(features_for_gating_and_experts, training=training) # Pass original features\n\n        flat_features_for_experts = jnp.reshape(features_for_gating_and_experts, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n        # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n        expert_outputs = []\n        for i in range(self.num_experts):\n            expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                input_dim=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                name=f'expert_{i}'\n            )\n            output_flat = expert_mlp(flat_features_for_experts, training=training)\n            expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n        expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n\
    \                                           (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n        expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n        expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n\n        moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n        final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n        neuron_biases = self.param(\n            'per_neuron_biases',\n            nn.initializers.zeros,\n            (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n        )\n\n        return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\nclass FullModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = None\n        self.num_neurons = None\n        self.input_horizon\
    \ = 4\n\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n        self.model = MoEWithSpatiallyAwareGating( # Updated class name here\n            mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n            input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n            neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n            temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n            temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size', 3),\n            spatial_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('spatial_kernel_size', 3),\n            num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4),\n            gating_hidden_dim=self.hparams.get('gating_hidden_dim', 32),\n            gating_cnn_features=self.hparams.get('gating_cnn_features',\
    \ 16),\n            gating_cnn_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('gating_cnn_kernel_size', 128),\n            gating_pool_window=self.hparams.get('gating_pool_window', 256)\n        )\n\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n \
    \           )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n        'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n        'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n        'spatial_kernel_size': 3,\n        'num_experts': 4,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32,\n        'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128,\n        'gating_pool_window': 256\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU\
    \ VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.010117\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 226943 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 226944\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_size': 128, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'neuron_embedding_dim': 8, 'temporal_conv_channels': 16, 'temporal_kernel_size': 3, 'spatial_kernel_size': 3, 'num_experts': 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, 'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE  \
    \ \n========================================\n   1    |   0.051517   |   0.030237  \n   2    |   0.030018   |   0.029755  \n   3    |   0.029432   |   0.029700  \n   4    |   0.029366   |   0.029336  \n   5    |   0.029219   |   0.029305  \n   6    |   0.029022   |   0.029214  \n   7    |   0.028936   |   0.029166  \n   8    |   0.028839   |   0.029011  \n   9    |   0.028751   |   0.029045  \n  10    |   0.028690   |   0.028926  \n========================================\nTimeout after 2827.9s at epoch 10\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2827.9s\nBest validation MAE: 0.028926\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.028926\nTraining time: 2840s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 226946\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_size': 128, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'neuron_embedding_dim': 8, 'temporal_conv_channels': 16, 'temporal_kernel_size': 3, 'spatial_kernel_size': 3, 'num_experts':\
    \ 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, 'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.051408   |   0.030822  \n   2    |   0.029826   |   0.029610  \n   3    |   0.029437   |   0.029534  \n   4    |   0.029316   |   0.029389  \n   5    |   0.029193   |   0.029469  \n   6    |   0.029096   |   0.029242  \n   7    |   0.028958   |   0.029189  \n   8    |   0.028866   |   0.029079  \n   9    |   0.028831   |   0.029293  \n  10    |   0.028740   |   0.029580  \n========================================\nTimeout after 2873.9s at epoch 10\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2873.9s\nBest validation MAE: 0.029079\n\
    \nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.029079\nTraining time: 2886s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 3dc2a4b4-e42d-4ed3-810b-59844205a559\nTotal time: 2963s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 21:42:36,415\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761226956415707157\n2025-10-23 21:42:36,466\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761226956466850038\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 138 | 1 | Veritas I: Revert to Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP (Regression Test) | Veritas I | 72 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 137 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993) + scale-invariant U/V orthonormal + γ prior | Ariadne I | 72 | -0.027020 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 136 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=34,H=96,a_max=0.993) + scale-invariant U/V orthonormal + γ prior | Ariadne I | 72 | -0.027044 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0290 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 135 | 1 | MoE: Spatial CNN Gating, Flattened Temporal CNN, Spatial CNN (Hidden), H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D... | Aether I | 71 | -0.029010 | 0.0200 | 0.0303 | 0.0322 | 0.0236 | 0.0269 |\n| 134 | 1 | Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM) | Logos I | 71 | -0.027334 | 0.0199 | 0.0285 | 0.0293 | 0.0233 | 0.0261\
    \ |\n| 133 | 1 | Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronEmbeddingMLP with Orthogonality Reg | Veritas I | 70 | -0.045146 | 0.0439 | 0.0391 | 0.0372 | 0.0492 | 0.0464 |\n| 132 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96) + V-OrthoReg + γ prior (λ_γ=1e-6) | Ariadne I | 70 | -0.026888 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 131 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=128, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 70 | -0.026930 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 130 | 1 | MoE: Revert to SOTA (ID 103), Adam, Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Glo... | Aether I | 70 | -0.027994 | 0.0202 | 0.0289 | 0.0311 | 0.0234 | 0.0263 |\n| 129 | 1 | Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm | Episteme I | 68 | -0.026743 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
