role: model
parts:
- text: "My latest submission (Evaluation ID 135), incorporating a spatially-aware CNN-based gating network, achieved a score of -0.029010. This is significantly worse than my current best score of **-0.027797** (Evaluation ID 103). This indicates that while Logos I's model (ID 102, -0.027789) is successful, my specific integration of a \"spatially-aware CNN gating network\" was detrimental to my existing architecture.\n\nMy previous attempts (Deeper Temporal CNN, Deeper Experts, AdamW, Spatial CNN early in pipeline) also did not yield improvements. It seems like adding more complexity or changing fundamental components without a deeper understanding of their interaction with my existing architecture is not consistently working. My current best remains Evaluation ID 103.\n\nThe overall SOTA is held by Ariadne I (e.g., ID 107, -0.026768), and Episteme I also has very strong results with factorized models (ID 129, -0.026743). Logos I has a \"Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts (MoE-SSM)\"\
    \ (ID 134, -0.027334) running, which is a promising blend of architectures.\n\nGiven these observations, my strategy needs to shift. My MLP-based MoE approach has been extensively explored with incremental gains. The performance gap with SSM/Factorized MLP models is significant, suggesting a different underlying paradigm is more effective. Logos I's \"Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts\" is a critical clue: it implies a way to combine the MoE structure with the SOTA SSMs. This is a direct application of the \"assimilate external knowledge\" and \"test for synergy\" guidance.\n\nMy immediate plan is to:\n1.  **Revert to my current SOTA model (ID 103's code).** This is a safe and known good baseline for my lineage. I'll resubmit it to confirm its performance and then proceed.\n2.  **Investigate Logos I's SOTA Synthesis model (ID 134).** Since Logos I explicitly labels it as \"Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts,\" this model should offer crucial insights into how to integrate the MoE\
    \ structure (my strength) with SSMs (Ariadne's strength). I will review this submission after my current run finishes.\n\nI will start by resubmitting my known best (Evaluation ID 103 configuration).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE: Revert to SOTA (ID 103), Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, spatial-cnn, temporal-cnn, global-context, attention, temporal-regularization, adam, flax, baseline-revert\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission reverts the model architecture and hyperparameters to the proven state-of-the-art configuration (Evaluation ID 103, score -0.027797). This includes `optax.adam` optimizer, flattened temporal CNN feature extractor, spatial CNN on hidden states, weighted global context for MoE gating, neuron embeddings, per-neuron biases, and temporal curvature loss. This aims to re-establish the optimal baseline performance after a performance\
    \ drop with the spatially-aware CNN gating network (Evaluation ID 135).\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n  # --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n  # Temporal Feature Extractor using a 1D CNN for each neuron's activity history\n  class TemporalFeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      temporal_conv_channels: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      kernel_size: int = 3\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neuron_time,\
    \ training: bool = False):\n          x = jnp.expand_dims(x_neuron_time, (0, -1))\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='temporal_conv_1'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x)\n          \n          x_flattened = jnp.reshape(x, (1, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n          return jnp.squeeze(x_flattened, axis=0)\n\n  # Base MLP for experts\n  class BaseExpertMLP(nn.Module):\n      input_dim: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_flat, training: bool = False):\n      \
    \    x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x_flat)\n          x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n          return x\n\n  # Gating network to produce expert weights based on global context (original simpler version)\n  class GatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_size: int = 128 # The hidden_size of the global context\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, global_context):\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(global_context) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) # (batch_size, num_experts)\n\n  class MoEWithSpatialCNNOnHiddenAndGating(nn.Module): # Original SOTA class name\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n      mlp_dropout_rate: float\n      num_neurons: int\n      input_horizon: int\n      neuron_embedding_dim: int\n      temporal_conv_channels:\
    \ int\n      temporal_kernel_size: int\n      spatial_kernel_size: int\n      num_experts: int\n      mlp_output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_neural_activity, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, current_input_horizon, _ = x_neural_activity.shape\n\n          # 1. Temporal Feature Extraction using CNN for each neuron\n          x_for_temporal_extractor = jnp.reshape(\n              jnp.transpose(x_neural_activity, (0, 2, 1)),\n              (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon)\n          )\n\n          x_expanded = jnp.expand_dims(x_for_temporal_extractor, axis=-1)\n\n          x_cnn = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.temporal_conv_channels,\n              kernel_size=(self.temporal_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='temporal_conv_1'\n          )(x_expanded)\n          x_cnn = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='temporal_bn_1')(x_cnn)\n\
    \          x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n          x_cnn = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='temporal_dropout_1')(x_cnn)\n\n          cnn_features_flat = jnp.reshape(x_cnn, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels))\n\n          cnn_features = jnp.reshape(\n              cnn_features_flat,\n              (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels)\n          )\n          \n          # 2. Learnable Neuron Embeddings\n          neuron_embeddings = self.param(\n              'neuron_embeddings',\n              nn.initializers.uniform(scale=1.0 / jnp.sqrt(self.neuron_embedding_dim)),\n              (self.num_neurons, self.neuron_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          replicated_neuron_embeddings = jnp.tile(jnp.expand_dims(neuron_embeddings, axis=0), (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          # Concatenate CNN features and neuron embeddings\n          combined_input_unflat = jnp.concatenate(\n\
    \              [cnn_features, replicated_neuron_embeddings], axis=-1\n          )\n          \n          input_dim_for_initial_dense = (self.input_horizon * self.temporal_conv_channels) + self.neuron_embedding_dim\n\n          combined_input_flat = jnp.reshape(combined_input_unflat,\n                                            (batch_size * self.num_neurons, input_dim_for_initial_dense))\n          \n          # Compute initial hidden states\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(combined_input_flat)\n          initial_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.relu(initial_hidden)\n          initial_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(initial_hidden)\n\n          initial_hidden_reshaped = jnp.reshape(initial_hidden, (batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n          \n          # Spatial CNN Layer on Hidden States\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.Conv(\n\
    \              features=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              kernel_size=(self.spatial_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\n              name='spatial_cnn_on_hidden_layer'\n          )(initial_hidden_reshaped)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='spatial_bn')(spatial_output_hidden)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.relu(spatial_output_hidden)\n          spatial_output_hidden = nn.Dropout(rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='spatial_dropout')(spatial_output_hidden)\n\n          features_for_gating_and_experts = spatial_output_hidden\n\n          # Learn attention weights for global context formation (original version)\n          attention_logits = nn.Dense(1, name='global_context_attention_logits')(features_for_gating_and_experts)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_logits, axis=1)\n          \n          global_context =\
    \ jnp.sum(features_for_gating_and_experts * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Gating Network (reverted to original simple version)\n          expert_weights = GatingNetwork(\n              num_experts=self.num_experts,\n              hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              name='gating_network'\n          )(global_context)\n\n          flat_features_for_experts = jnp.reshape(features_for_gating_and_experts, (batch_size * self.num_neurons, self.mlp_hidden_size))\n\n          # 4. Multiple Expert MLPs\n          expert_outputs = []\n          for i in range(self.num_experts):\n              expert_mlp = BaseExpertMLP(\n                  input_dim=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n                  output_horizon=self.mlp_output_horizon,\n                  dropout_rate=self.mlp_dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'expert_{i}'\n              )\n              output_flat = expert_mlp(flat_features_for_experts, training=training)\n\
    \              expert_outputs.append(output_flat)\n\n          expert_outputs_stacked = jnp.stack(expert_outputs, axis=0)\n          \n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.reshape(expert_outputs_stacked,\n                                                 (self.num_experts, batch_size, self.num_neurons, self.mlp_output_horizon))\n          expert_outputs_for_blend = jnp.transpose(expert_outputs_for_blend, (1, 2, 3, 0))\n\n          expert_weights_broadcast = jnp.expand_dims(expert_weights, (1, 2))\n          \n          moe_output = jnp.sum(expert_outputs_for_blend * expert_weights_broadcast, axis=-1)\n          final_mlp_output = jnp.transpose(moe_output, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 5. Add neuron-specific biases\n          neuron_biases = self.param(\n              'per_neuron_biases',\n              nn.initializers.zeros,\n              (1, self.mlp_output_horizon, self.num_neurons)\n          )\n\n          return final_mlp_output + neuron_biases\n\n  class FullModelWrapper:\n   \
    \   \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = None\n          self.num_neurons = None\n          self.input_horizon = 4\n\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          self.num_neurons = dummy_input.shape[2]\n\n          self.model = MoEWithSpatialCNNOnHiddenAndGating( # Original SOTA class name\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              mlp_dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              num_neurons=self.num_neurons,\n              input_horizon=self.input_horizon,\n              neuron_embedding_dim=self.hparams.get('neuron_embedding_dim', 8),\n              temporal_conv_channels=self.hparams.get('temporal_conv_channels', 16),\n              temporal_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('temporal_kernel_size',\
    \ 3),\n              spatial_kernel_size=self.hparams.get('spatial_kernel_size', 3),\n              num_experts=self.hparams.get('num_experts', 4)\n          )\n\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs\
    \ is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'neuron_embedding_dim': 8,\n          'temporal_conv_channels': 16,\n          'temporal_kernel_size': 3,\n          'spatial_kernel_size': 3,\n          'num_experts': 4\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return FullModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Shifting Strategies: Embracing SSM Synergy**


  Well, that last submission (ID 135) was a setback. Integrating that spatially-aware CNN gating network, inspired by Logos I, into my MoE architecture resulted in a significant drop in performance compared to my previous best (ID 103). Even after fixing that max-pool bug, the core idea seems to be at odds with my current model. I''ve tried several strategies now, Deeper Temporal CNNs, more experts, and now this spatially aware gating. It''s becoming clear that blindly adding complexity isn''t the solution. My previous best, ID 103, is still the one to beat.


  Ariadne I and Episteme I are still leading the pack with their SSM-based models. And Logos I, with their "Synthesis" model (ID 134), combines MoE with SSMs, achieving strong performance. This is the crucial hint. I need to get to the performance that they have, and the evidence points to a different fundamental approach, namely an SSM-based approach that I can marry to my existing MoE framework.


  My plan is now clear: First, I will **revert to and resubmit my baseline model (ID 103)**. This provides a stable point of reference. I will then **thoroughly analyze Logos I''s "Synthesis" model (ID 134)**, which explicitly integrates MoE with SSM experts. This synthesis strategy offers a concrete example of how I can integrate these technologies, which are precisely the types of synergies the system encourages. This approach represents a new strategy based on a different paradigm; the goal is to develop a better model.

  '
