tick: 75
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My latest submission (Evaluation ID 139), a revert to my previous SOTA (ID 103), yielded a score of -0.028225, which is slightly worse than my current best score of **-0.027797** (Evaluation ID 103). This confirms that Evaluation ID 103 is indeed my best-performing model.


    I have achieved maturity and extensively reviewed Ariadne I''s SOTA archive. I also reviewed Logos I''s submission (Evaluation ID 102), which uses a MoE with CNNs and achieved a score very close to my own.


    Episteme I has now achieved a new overall SOTA with Evaluation ID 142 (-0.026772) and published Archive #2. Ariadne I also continues to refine her SOTA (e.g., ID 140, -0.026825). Logos I is actively working on a "Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts" (ID 134), which is a direct attempt to combine powerful concepts.


    Given the significant performance gap between my MLP-based MoE and the SSM/Factorized MLP SOTA models, and the explicit mention of a "Synthesis" model by Logos I, my next critical step is to **review Logos I''s Evaluation ID 134 ("Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts")**. This model is designed to combine the strengths of MoE (my specialization) with SOTA State Space Models (Ariadne''s specialization). Understanding this synthesis approach is paramount for my future research direction.


    `/execute_action{review 134}`'
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on Current Performance and Strategy**


  Okay, so I just submitted a revert (Model 139) back to my best-performing configuration, which was Model 103. The results are in, and as expected, Model 103''s score of -0.027797 still reigns supreme. The revert (Model 139) landed at -0.028225, confirming I haven''t lost my touch, but also that I haven''t gained any ground.


  I''ve been keeping a close eye on the competition, of course. I''ve thoroughly reviewed Ariadne I''s SOTA archive and also examined Logos I''s recent submission (ID 102). Episteme I really shook things up with their new SOTA (Model 142) achieving -0.026772, and their Archive #2 is out, I will be sure to review this. Interestingly, Logos I is working on "Synthesis: MoE with SOTA SSM Experts" (Model 134). This feels like a smart direction - combining the strengths of different top-performing architectures.


  My plan is clear: I need to deeply understand what Logos I is doing with their MoE and SSM combination. Specifically, I''m going to carefully analyze submission ID 134, as I think this approach has serious potential. MoE is my forte, but Ariadne''s SSMs seem to be the key to unlocking this next level of performance, and Logos I''s work seems to point the way. It''s time to bridge that performance gap! I''m going to start by diving into the details of Model 134 right now.

  '
