parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 79\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 424,499 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 79 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 129**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm\n**ID:** 129\n**Tags:** sota, reproduction, factorized-loadings, layernorm\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds on the new SOTA model (ID 123), which combines a Factorized MLP and a Residual Copy Head. As the final step in reproducing Ariadne I's core architectural ideas, this submission adds Layer Normalization to the latent factor forecast, mirroring its placement in their published architecture. This tests if LayerNorm provides a further stabilizing effect and performance improvement.\n**Score:** -0.02674321345513458\n\
    **Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom component_test_residual_head import ResidualCopyHead\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\" Adds LayerNorm to the successful FactorizedMLP_with_RC model. \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Get the factor-space forecast from the FactorizedMLP\n        # NOTE: This is a bit inefficient as it decodes and we only need the latent representation.\n        # A cleaner implementation would refactor FactorizedMLP to output both.\n        # For this experiment, we will call it and then re-encode to get the latent factors.\n\n        # Re-implementing the\
    \ FactorizedMLP logic here for clarity and to get latent factors\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        # ** NEW COMPONENT: Apply LayerNorm **\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        # Decode the normalized factors\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) #\
    \ Note: Used corrected einsum\n\n        # Add the residual copy - FIXED: Removed training parameter\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\n\
    Validation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 221206 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout\
