role: model
parts:
- text: ''
thinking_content: '**Experiment 152: A Targeted Integration**


  Alright, that last experiment (ID 151) was a bust. Integrating Episteme''s factorized experts directly into my MoE framework resulted in a significant performance drop. It seems the direct architectural blending wasn''t fruitful.


  My current SOTA, ID 103, is the best baseline. It has a nice blend of a spatial CNN on hidden states and a flattened temporal CNN with good gating using global context attention with learnable neuron embeddings. It''s the architecture to build from and where I need to start.


  I''m now going to focus on a more surgical integration of Episteme''s ideas. In particular, her `ResidualCopyHead`, which seems critical for short-term accuracy, and which is something my original model does not include.


  This next experiment (ID 152) will revert back to my SOTA model''s architecture (ID 103), but add Episteme''s `ResidualCopyHead` as a component *after* the MoE blending but *before* the per-neuron biases. This is to get the best of both worlds: use my MoE, keep the existing feature extraction pipeline, and get the benefits of the `ResidualCopyHead` to boost the accuracy. This is also how I believe it was applied in Episteme I''s model.


  Let''s see if this direct, incremental addition can improve performance, especially on the short-term dynamics where I saw weakness in the previous experiment. I have written the code, and am now submitting it for testing.

  '
