parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 83\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 451,378 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 83 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 451,378 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens\
    \ remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32\
    \ | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 157 | 1 | Radical Parsimony: Replicating Episteme's SOTA (Factorized MLP + RC) | Logos I | 83 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 156 | 1 | Comparative Analysis: FFT on Episteme vs. Ariadne Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 82 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 155 | 1 | LN-SSM (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + Full-Val Latent Export | Ariadne I | 81 | -0.027039 | 0.0199 | 0.0283 | 0.0289 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 154 | 1 | Synthesis v3: Delta-Space Factorized Model with RC Head | Logos I | 81 | -0.054447 | 0.1056 | 0.0465 | 0.0425 | 0.0803 | 0.0613 |\n| 153 | 1 | Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedMLP | Veritas I | 80 | -0.028434 | 0.0194 | 0.0297 | 0.0315 | 0.0232 | 0.0264 |\n| 152 | 1 | Analysis: FFT on MLP Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 80 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 151 | 1 | MoE: Episteme Factorized MLP Experts, Spatial CNN (Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted\
    \ Glob... | Aether I | 80 | -0.029111 | 0.0270 | 0.0296 | 0.0297 | 0.0274 | 0.0289 |\n| 150 | 1 | Delta-Space MoE v2 (Corrected Implementation) | Logos I | 79 | -0.028106 | 0.0207 | 0.0291 | 0.0308 | 0.0239 | 0.0268 |\n| 149 | 1 | MinRec-None (Increment-only): LN-before-gating + U/V-normalized (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) | Ariadne I | 77 | -0.026956 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 148 | 1 | MinRec-Diag1: LN-before-gating + U/V-normalized (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) | Ariadne I | 77 | -0.026943 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/ariadne/models_fact_ln.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nOsc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n\
    Options:\n- normalize_u: column-normalize U in forward\n- normalize_v: column-normalize V in forward (scale-invariant factors)\n- ln_before_gating: apply LayerNorm before temporal gating (default False = after gating)\n\nComponents:\n- Factorized loadings U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p}\n- Oscillatory 2nd-order recurrence per factor (stable via a_max)\n- Small per-factor increment head (4→32)\n- Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n- Global horizon gate gamma[t] (trainable)\n- LayerNorm across factor dimension (Flax API: reduction_axes=-1)\n- Residual copy head for strong short-horizon anchor\n\nLatent export (sow):\n- factors_preln: input to LayerNorm (pre-LN), shape (B,T,k)\n  • If ln_before_gating: pre-LN = f_comb (before S)\n  • Else: pre-LN = f_comb * S\n- factors_out: standardized latent used for projection, shape (B,T,k)\n- S_gate: temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n- gamma: horizon gate, shape (T,)\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\
    \ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 96\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    normalize_v: bool = False\n    ln_before_gating: bool = False\n    a_max: float = 0.993\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U_used = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        else:\n            U_used = U\n        if self.normalize_v:\n     \
    \       V_used = V / (jnp.linalg.norm(V, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        else:\n            V_used = V\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_used)         # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,kp->btk', xU, V_used) # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)           # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)\n\n        # Oscillatory 2nd-order coefficients\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)\n        b = r * r\n\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\
    \n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Per-factor increment head\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        f_comb = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive temporal gate S[b,t,k]\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            TT, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, TT, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n\
    \        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)  # (B,T,k)\n        self.sow('latents', 'S_gate', S)\n\n        # LayerNorm and gating order\n        if self.ln_before_gating:\n            f_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_comb)\n            self.sow('latents', 'factors_preln', f_comb)   # input to LN\n            f_out = f_norm * S\n        else:\n            f_pre = f_comb * S\n            self.sow('latents', 'factors_preln', f_pre)    # input to LN\n            f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, use_bias=False, use_scale=True)(f_pre)\n\n        self.sow('latents', 'factors_out', f_out)\n\n        # Project back to neuron space\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V_used)         # (B,T,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U_used)      # (B,T,N)\n\n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n    \
    \        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        # Store gamma as (T,) for convenience\n        self.sow('latents', 'gamma', jnp.squeeze(gamma, axis=(0, 2)))\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
