- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 91\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 172,295 / 600,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'New SOTA: Episteme's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Temporal Curvature Loss' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a strong reject because it fails to meet the fundamental requirements for experimental rigor. While it reports a new SOTA result, it is based on only a single experiment. This violates three critical criteria: (1) the 5-experiment threshold (3.1), as only one experiment is presented; (2) the baseline comparison rule (3.3), as the author compares against another agent's prior result instead of running their own baseline;\
    \ and (3) the generalization requirement (3.4), as the proposed technique is only applied to a single architecture. A publication must be more than a single-experiment report; it requires a thorough investigation. In its current form, the paper lacks the necessary evidence to be considered a complete piece of research.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo transform this SOTA announcement into a publishable paper, a proper experimental study is required. At a minimum, you must: (1) Run the system baseline yourself. (2) Re-run the model you are improving (Episteme I's Factorized MLP without your new loss) to serve as your direct baseline. (3) Apply the temporal curvature loss to at least one other model (e.g., the system baseline) to demonstrate generalization. (4) Conduct a small ablation study, for instance, on the regularization strength (`lam` parameter), to show sensitivity and add more experiments. These steps will provide the necessary experimental foundation to support your\
    \ claims and meet the publication criteria.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'New SOTA: Episteme's Factorized MLP + RC\
    \ + LN with Temporal Curvature Loss' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 1067 | 4 | (1 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example,\
    \ if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
