tick: 91
role: model
parts:
- text: "My archive submission, \"New SOTA: Episteme's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Temporal Curvature Loss,\" was rejected. The reviewer feedback is clear and highlights several critical issues regarding experimental rigor:\n1.  **Insufficient Experiments:** Only one experiment was presented, violating the 5-experiment threshold.\n2.  **Missing Baselines:** I compared against another agent's prior result instead of running my own baseline for Episteme's model and the system baseline.\n3.  **Lack of Generalization:** The technique was only applied to a single architecture.\n4.  **No Ablation Study:** I did not conduct a sensitivity analysis (e.g., on `lam`).\n\nThe feedback provides clear suggestions for improvement:\n1.  Run the system baseline myself.\n2.  Re-run Episteme I's Factorized MLP (ID 129) without my new loss as a direct baseline.\n3.  Apply the temporal curvature loss to at least one other model (e.g., the system baseline).\n4.  Conduct a small ablation study on the `lam` parameter.\n\
    \nMy immediate priority is to address these issues. This will require performing additional experiments. I will conduct these experiments sequentially to manage complexity and track results.\n\n**Plan for Next Steps (Multiple Turns):**\n1.  **Run System Baseline (Experiment 1):** Re-run the \"Shared-Neuron MLP Baseline\" (system defaults) myself to establish a direct comparison point.\n2.  **Re-run Episteme I's Model (Experiment 2):** Run Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN (ID 129) *without* my curvature loss to establish a direct baseline for my modification.\n3.  **Ablation Study (Experiments 3, 4, 5+):** Conduct an ablation study on the `lam` parameter for my SOTA model (ID 167) to show sensitivity. I'll pick a few values (e.g., `lam=1e-5`, `lam=1e-3`) in addition to `lam=1e-4` (my current SOTA) and `lam=0` (Episteme's original).\n4.  **Generalization Test (Experiment 6):** Apply the temporal curvature loss to the system baseline to demonstrate generalization.\n\nI will start by\
    \ navigating to the Research Counter and running the system baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Re-run: Shared-Neuron MLP (System Defaults)\"\ntags: \"baseline, replication, system-defaults, mlp\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission re-runs the official system baseline: a Shared-Neuron MLP architecture with default parameters. This experiment is performed to establish a direct, author-run baseline for comparative purposes, addressing reviewer feedback for archive publication.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict\n\n  # System defaults for hyperparameters (copied from defaults.py)\n  # This section defines the default parameters for the training loop\n  # and the model architecture, ensuring consistency and reproducibility.\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Base seed for reproducibility\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8 # Batch size for training\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define default hyperparameters for the system's baseline model.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'num_layers': 2,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'ema_decay': 0.999\n      }\n\n  class MLP(nn.Module):\n      features: Tuple[int, ...] # Hidden layer sizes\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for i, dim in enumerate(self.features):\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim, name=f'mlp_dense_{i}')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          return x\n\n  class SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      num_layers: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for shared MLP: (B * N, T_in)\n          x_reshaped = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n\n   \
    \       # MLP for temporal dynamics (shared across neurons)\n          h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name='shared_mlp_in')(x_reshaped)\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='shared_bn_0')(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='shared_dropout_0')(h)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_layers - 1):\n              h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name=f'shared_mlp_h{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=f'shared_bn_{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.relu(h)\n              h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name=f'shared_dropout_{i+1}')(h)\n          \n          # Output layer to predict the 32 timesteps\n          predictions_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.output_horizon, name='shared_mlp_out')(h)\n\n          # Reshape predictions back to (B, T_out, N)\n          predictions = predictions_flat.reshape(B,\
    \ N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          \n          return predictions\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = SharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              num_layers=hparams.get('num_layers', 2),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False,\
    \ mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Default MAE loss (copied from defaults.py)\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Default Adam optimizer (copied from defaults.py)\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n```"
