parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 93\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 178,546 / 600,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Baseline Re-run: Shared-Neuron MLP (System Defaults)' (ID: 173) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029863062711975457\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0238\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0312\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0336\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 173\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been fixed and is running without crashing. The\
    \ submission ran successfully for 301+ seconds, significantly exceeding the monitor timeout of 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a missing import in the type annotations. Specifically, the code used `Tuple[int, ...]` as a type annotation in the `MLP` class (line 27) but failed to import `Tuple` from the `typing` module.\n\nThe error was:\n```\nNameError: name 'Tuple' is not defined. Did you mean: 'tuple'?\n```\n\nThis occurred because the imports on line 5 only included:\n```python\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n```\n\nBut the code required `Tuple` for the type annotation:\n```python\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\n    features: Tuple[int, ...]  # Hidden layer sizes\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version:** submission_v2.py\n\n**Change:** Added `Tuple` to the typing imports on line 5.\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n```\n\nThis was a simple one-line fix that resolved the import error.\
    \ No other changes were needed.\n\n## Verification\n- The monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py has been running for 301+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- The evaluation system accepted the submission and is processing it\n- Original submission crashed immediately on import; fixed version runs successfully\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and working. The code now imports all required typing annotations and can execute without errors. The submission is ready for full evaluation by the research system.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n# System defaults for hyperparameters (copied from defaults.py)\n# This section defines the default parameters for the\
    \ training loop\n# and the model architecture, ensuring consistency and reproducibility.\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Base seed for reproducibility\nBATCH_SIZE = 8 # Batch size for training\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define default hyperparameters for the system's baseline model.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_size': 128,\n        'num_layers': 2,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'ema_decay': 0.999\n    }\n\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\n    features: Tuple[int, ...] # Hidden layer sizes\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        for i, dim in enumerate(self.features):\n            x = nn.Dense(features=dim, name=f'mlp_dense_{i}')(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n        return x\n\nclass SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n    num_layers: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n\
    \        # Reshape input for shared MLP: (B * N, T_in)\n        x_reshaped = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n\n        # MLP for temporal dynamics (shared across neurons)\n        h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name='shared_mlp_in')(x_reshaped)\n        h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='shared_bn_0')(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='shared_dropout_0')(h)\n\n        for i in range(self.num_layers - 1):\n            h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name=f'shared_mlp_h{i+1}')(h)\n            h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=f'shared_bn_{i+1}')(h)\n            h = nn.relu(h)\n            h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name=f'shared_dropout_{i+1}')(h)\n\n        # Output layer to predict the 32 timesteps\n        predictions_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.output_horizon, name='shared_mlp_out')(h)\n\n       \
    \ # Reshape predictions back to (B, T_out, N)\n        predictions = predictions_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        return predictions\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    \"\"\"\n    Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = SharedNeuronMLP(\n            hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n            num_layers=hparams.get('num_layers', 2),\n            dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n \
    \   def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # Default MAE loss (copied from defaults.py)\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    # Default Adam optimizer (copied from defaults.py)\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\n```\n\
