role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 94\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 187,166 / 600,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 94 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Baseline Re-run: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN (No Curvature Loss)' (ID: 176) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02683748925927105\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0258\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0287\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 176\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the missing hyperparameters function that caused a KeyError during model initialization.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code defined a custom neural\
    \ network model `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` that requires two hyperparameters:\n- `rank_k`: Latent factor dimension\n- `proj_rank`: Projection dimension\n\nHowever, the submission was missing the `_define_hyperparameters()` function. When the evaluation system loaded the code, it fell back to the default hyperparameters function which only defines `{'learning_rate': 0.001}`. This caused a `KeyError: 'rank_k'` when the `ModelWrapper.__init__` method tried to access these missing keys.\n\n**Error from original submission:**\n```\nFile \"submission.py\", line 86, in __init__\n    rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n           ~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^\nKeyError: 'rank_k'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the `_define_hyperparameters()` function to the submission (submission_v2.py) that defines all required hyperparameters:\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the FactorizedMLP model with ResidualCopyHead.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'rank_k': 16,  # Latent factor\
    \ dimension\n        'proj_rank': 64,  # Projection dimension\n        'learning_rate': 0.001\n    }\n```\n\nThis ensures that when the evaluation system calls `funcs['define_hyperparameters']()`, it returns a dictionary with all the keys that the model expects, preventing the KeyError.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitoring script (`monitor_evaluation.py`), which confirmed that:\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- No new errors were encountered during execution\n- The submission is successfully running (though taking longer than the monitor timeout to complete the full evaluation)\n\n## Implementation Details\nThe hyperparameter values chosen (`rank_k=16`, `proj_rank=64`) are reasonable defaults for this type of factorized model architecture. These values should allow the model to run the validation and full training process without issues.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies\
    \ on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Default MAE loss (no curvature)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n# Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py)\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Copies the 4 input steps to the first 4 output steps and adds a\n    learned residual for the full 32-step horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch, 4, num_neurons)\n\n        # Simple MLP to learn the full 32-step residual\n        # Reshape for MLP: (batch * num_neurons, 4)\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual\
    \ = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) # Predicts a 32-step residual\n\n        # Reshape residual back to: (batch, 32, num_neurons)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Create the full 32-step output scaffold\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n\n        # Copy input x to the first 4 steps of the output\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n\n        # Add the learned residual to the full output\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n# Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (from ID 129)\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32 # Fixed by task\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n\
    \        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) # Column normalization of U\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U) # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T) # (B,4,k)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat) # Episteme uses 512\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        # Add dropout here, consistent with general practice and previous Aether I models.\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n\n        # Apply LayerNorm\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        # Decode the normalized factors\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn',\
    \ z, U)\n\n        # Add the residual copy\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats'] # Includes batch_stats for any potential BatchNorm in ResidualCopyHead\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n\
    \                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the FactorizedMLP model with ResidualCopyHead.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'rank_k': 16,  # Latent factor dimension\n        'proj_rank': 64,  # Projection dimension\n        'learning_rate': 0.001\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 256914 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 256916\nHyperparameters: {'rank_k': 16, 'proj_rank': 64, 'learning_rate': 0.001}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030994   |   0.029580  \n   2    |   0.028890   |   0.029472  \n   3    |   0.028361   |   0.028445  \n   4    |   0.027725   |\
    \   0.028515  \n   5    |   0.027360   |   0.027994  \n   6    |   0.026980   |   0.027717  \n   7    |   0.026578   |   0.027643  \n   8    |   0.026313   |   0.027596  \n   9    |   0.026074   |   0.027046  \n  10    |   0.025870   |   0.027127  \n  11    |   0.025724   |   0.027166  \n  12    |   0.025672   |   0.027473  \n  13    |   0.025549   |   0.026957  \n  14    |   0.025428   |   0.027186  \n  15    |   0.025414   |   0.027379  \n  16    |   0.025327   |   0.027480  \n  17    |   0.025203   |   0.027046  \n  18    |   0.025169   |   0.027300  \n  19    |   0.025143   |   0.026982  \n  20    |   0.025085   |   0.027072  \n  21    |   0.025033   |   0.026933  \n  22    |   0.025018   |   0.026998  \n  23    |   0.024988   |   0.027193  \n  24    |   0.024944   |   0.026965  \n  25    |   0.024927   |   0.027047  \n  26    |   0.024899   |   0.027309  \n  27    |   0.024898   |   0.026925  \n  28    |   0.024860   |   0.027076  \n  29    |   0.024840   |   0.027195  \n  30  \
    \  |   0.024822   |   0.026903  \n  31    |   0.024825   |   0.027130  \n  32    |   0.024837   |   0.027059  \n  33    |   0.024791   |   0.027432  \n  34    |   0.024784   |   0.027222  \n  35    |   0.024765   |   0.027059  \n  36    |   0.024754   |   0.027082  \n  37    |   0.024746   |   0.027290  \n  38    |   0.024747   |   0.027019  \n  39    |   0.024736   |   0.027055  \n  40    |   0.024730   |   0.026976  \n  41    |   0.024698   |   0.027109  \n  42    |   0.024717   |   0.027032  \n  43    |   0.024704   |   0.026940  \n  44    |   0.024692   |   0.026980  \n  45    |   0.024687   |   0.026920  \n  46    |   0.024677   |   0.027102  \n  47    |   0.024666   |   0.027097  \n  48    |   0.024691   |   0.026989  \n  49    |   0.024654   |   0.027124  \n  50    |   0.024638   |   0.026951  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 50 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2402.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026903\n\
