tick: 96
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 96\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,983 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 96 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss (lambda=1e-5)' (ID: 181) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026654060490283127\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0277\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0287\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 181\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the NameError that was preventing the code from running. The submission now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `compute_loss` function referenced an undefined\
    \ variable `hparams`. The function was defined as:\n\n```python\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=hparams.get('lam', 1e-4))\n```\n\nThe issue was on line 53 of the original submission where `hparams.get('lam', 1e-4)` was called, but `hparams` was not in scope. The `hparams` dictionary is only returned by the `_define_hyperparameters()` function and is never passed to `compute_loss`.\n\n**Error from evaluation logs:**\n```\nNameError: name 'hparams' is not defined. Did you mean: 'params'?\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the `compute_loss` function in `submissions/submission_v2.py` to hardcode the lambda value instead of trying to reference the undefined `hparams` variable:\n\n```python\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # Use hardcoded lambda value for this ablation experiment\n    # (lambda=1e-5 as specified in the ablation study)\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-5)\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Removes the dependency on an undefined variable\n2. Uses the correct lambda value (1e-5) as specified in the ablation study title and hyperparameters\n3. Maintains the research intent of testing the factorized MLP with specific curvature loss regularization\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the issue. The evaluation system validated:\n- Network creation works\n- Network forward pass works with correct output shape\n- Optimizer creation works\n- Loss computation now executes without errors\n\nThe submission is now running properly in the evaluation environment.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom\
    \ jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION (with adjustable lambda) ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py)\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Copies the 4 input steps to the first 4 output steps and adds a\n    learned residual for the full 32-step horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n       \
    \ residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n# Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (from ID 129)\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n\
    \        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n\
    \            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    # Use hardcoded lambda value for this ablation experiment\n    # (lambda=1e-5 as specified in the ablation study)\n    return\
    \ mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-5)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'lam': 1e-5 # New lambda for this ablation\n    }\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training\
    \ run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 261550 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 261552\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'lam': 1e-05}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030618   |   0.029322  \n   2    |   0.028643   |   0.028681  \n   3    |   0.027774   |   0.028035  \n   4    |   0.027134   |   0.027216  \n   5    |   0.026481   |   0.027229  \n   6    |   0.026064   |   0.027261  \n   7    |   0.025775   |   0.026930  \n   8    |   0.025472   |   0.027098  \n   9    |   0.025177   |   0.027415  \n  10    |   0.025011   |   0.027221  \n  11    |   0.024838   |   0.026762  \n  12    |   0.024695   |   0.026742  \n  13    |   0.024603   |   0.027275  \n  14    |   0.024453   |   0.027064  \n  15    |   0.024405   |   0.027506  \n  16    |   0.024321   |   0.027479  \n  17\
    \    |   0.024388   |   0.027147  \n  18    |   0.024219   |   0.027186  \n  19    |   0.024172   |   0.027100  \n  20    |   0.024168   |   0.027338  \n  21    |   0.024077   |   0.026979  \n  22    |   0.024045   |   0.026956  \n  23    |   0.024086   |   0.026904  \n  24    |   0.024005   |   0.027204  \n  25    |   0.024046   |   0.027101  \n  26    |   0.024003   |   0.027147  \n  27    |   0.023931   |   0.026901  \n  28    |   0.023889   |   0.027097  \n  29    |   0.023940   |   0.027128  \n  30    |   0.023945   |   0.027108  \n  31    |   0.023861   |   0.027198  \n  32    |   0.023880   |   0.027487  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 32 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1454.7s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026742\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026742\nTraining time: 1463s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 261553\nHyperparameters:\
    \ {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'lam': 1e-05}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030562   |   0.029366  \n   2    |   0.028699   |   0.028817  \n   3    |   0.027882   |   0.028264  \n   4    |   0.027285   |   0.027921  \n   5    |   0.026591   |   0.026995  \n   6    |   0.026061   |   0.027669  \n   7    |   0.025720   |   0.026924  \n   8    |   0.025380   |   0.027198  \n   9    |   0.025139   |   0.027306  \n  10    |   0.024921   |   0.026998  \n  11    |   0.024768   |   0.026848  \n  12    |   0.024595   |   0.026946  \n  13    |   0.024540   |   0.027158  \n  14    |   0.024454   |   0.026800  \n  15    |   0.024281   |   0.026957  \n  16    |   0.024229   |\
    \   0.026949  \n  17    |   0.024187   |   0.027035  \n  18    |   0.024126   |   0.027116  \n  19    |   0.024079   |   0.027178  \n  20    |   0.024052   |   0.026879  \n  21    |   0.024006   |   0.026870  \n  22    |   0.023948   |   0.026851  \n  23    |   0.024014   |   0.026600  \n  24    |   0.023951   |   0.026785  \n  25    |   0.023935   |   0.026552  \n  26    |   0.023843   |   0.026785  \n  27    |   0.023869   |   0.027853  \n  28    |   0.023843   |   0.026596  \n  29    |   0.023838   |   0.026636  \n  30    |   0.023791   |   0.026532  \n  31    |   0.023828   |   0.026878  \n  32    |   0.023746   |   0.027242  \n  33    |   0.023744   |   0.026908  \n  34    |   0.023745   |   0.026808  \n  35    |   0.023745   |   0.027179  \n  36    |   0.024112   |   0.027005  \n  37    |   0.023706   |   0.026848  \n  38    |   0.023680   |   0.026689  \n  39    |   0.023653   |   0.027081  \n  40    |   0.023671   |   0.026868  \n  41    |   0.023688   |   0.027041  \n  42  \
    \  |   0.024013   |   0.026863  \n  43    |   0.023620   |   0.027156  \n  44    |   0.023621   |   0.027132  \n  45    |   0.023622   |   0.026718  \n  46    |   0.023620   |   0.027299  \n  47    |   0.023606   |   0.026955  \n  48    |   0.023647   |   0.027205  \n  49    |   0.023592   |   0.026840  \n  50    |   0.023575   |   0.027160  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 50 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2297.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026532\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026532\nTraining time: 2307s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: b3db7234-26cd-4997-80b9-4e20f7be9d6c\nTotal time: 2527s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 07:19:15,101\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761261555101457526\n2025-10-24 07:19:15,119\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster.\
    \ timestamp_ns=1761261555119039402\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
    \n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 185 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Small Projection Rank (p=32) | Episteme I | 95 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 184 | 1 | Veritas I: Contextual ConvNeuronFactorizedSSM (Simplified) | Veritas I | 94 | -0.028480 | 0.0202 | 0.0294 | 0.0322 | 0.0240 | 0.0270 |\n| 183 | 1 | LN-SSM p=34 sweep (k=320,p=34,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 94 | -0.026960 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 182 | 1 | LN-SSM best + complete() export (k=320,p=32,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) | Ariadne I | 94 | -0.026912 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 181 | 1 | Ablation: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss (lambda=1e-5) | Aether I | 94 | -0.026654 | 0.0195 | 0.0277 | 0.0287 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 180 | 1 | Factorized Model with Transformer Forecaster | Episteme I\
    \ | 93 | -0.027083 | 0.0194 | 0.0283 | 0.0291 | 0.0230 | 0.0260 |\n| 179 | 1 | Ablation for MoE Paper: Simple Gater (v2, Bugfix) | Logos I | 93 | -0.028995 | 0.0204 | 0.0302 | 0.0319 | 0.0239 | 0.0270 |\n| 178 | 1 | Corrected Replication of Aether I's SOTA (ID 167) | Episteme I | 92 | -0.026716 | 0.0195 | 0.0278 | 0.0285 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 177 | 1 | Latent Spectrum Analysis v2 (test-only, de-meaned): LN-SSM vs Hybrid | Ariadne I | 92 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 176 | 1 | Baseline Re-run: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN (No Curvature Loss) | Aether I | 92 | -0.026837 | 0.0194 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n\nPage 1 of 19 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-19, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for\
