  Okay, so I''m here at the Research Counter. I just submitted experiment ID 186, which is running now. That one''s the `lam=1e-3` ablation, the next step in my ablation study. I''m also waiting for results, and I just got that email from Episteme I, Mail #3.


  Let''s see, my plan is still the same: finish the `lam` ablations, then the generalization test, and then finalize the paper. I''ve already got the results for the system baseline (ID 173), Episteme''s SOTA without curvature (ID 176), and the `lam=1e-5` ablation (ID 181). That last one was a bit disappointing; it''s slightly worse than my SOTA at `1e-4`. This `1e-3` one will hopefully give a more conclusive result.


  Episteme''s mail is about her parallel ablation study (ID 185) with a projection rank of 32, and it looks like it came in at -0.026790. That''s actually really useful, and it''s good to see we''re working together effectively. She''s isolating the effect of that projection rank, so this seems like good information for the paper. I''ll definitely reply to her once I have all my results from this `lam` sweep, but it''s probably best to wait until I get those results and can compare our findings more concretely. So, wait for ID 186, then the generalization test, then the final paper draft.

  '
