tick: 98
role: model
parts:
- text: "My ablation experiment for `lam=1e-3` (Evaluation ID 186) has completed with a score of -0.026661. This result is slightly worse than both my SOTA (ID 167, `lam=1e-4`, score -0.026638) and the `lam=1e-5` ablation (ID 181, score -0.026654). This reinforces `lam=1e-4` as the optimal regularization strength among the tested values, with `lam=1e-5` and `lam=1e-3` yielding slightly inferior results.\n\nI have now completed four experiments for my publication, addressing the reviewer's feedback for the ablation study:\n1.  **System Baseline (ID 173):** Score -0.029863 (Baseline Comparison)\n2.  **Episteme's SOTA (without curvature loss) (ID 176):** Score -0.026837 (Direct Baseline Comparison)\n3.  **Ablation `lam=1e-5` (ID 181):** Score -0.026654\n4.  **Ablation `lam=1e-3` (ID 186):** Score -0.026661\n5.  **My SOTA (ID 167):** Score -0.026638 (Implicit `lam=1e-4` point for ablation curve)\n\nI still need to conduct one more experiment to address the \"generalization requirement\" by applying\
    \ the temporal curvature loss to another model (the system baseline).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization: System Baseline with Temporal Curvature Loss (lambda=1e-4)\"\ntags: \"generalization, system-baseline, mlp, temporal-regularization, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission aims to demonstrate the broader applicability of the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss function by integrating it into the standard Shared-Neuron MLP baseline architecture. Using a `lambda` value of 1e-4 (the optimal strength identified in previous ablations), this experiment tests if the curvature regularization provides similar performance benefits in a different model, addressing reviewer feedback for archive publication regarding generalization.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION (with adjustable lambda)\
    \ ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # System defaults for hyperparameters (copied from defaults.py)\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Base seed for reproducibility\n  BATCH_SIZE = 8 # Batch size for training\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'num_layers': 2,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'ema_decay': 0.999,\n          'lam': 1e-4 # Lambda for curvature loss\n      }\n\n  class MLP(nn.Module):\n      features: Tuple[int, ...]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for i, dim in enumerate(self.features):\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim, name=f'mlp_dense_{i}')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          return x\n\n  class SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      num_layers: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_reshaped = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name='shared_mlp_in')(x_reshaped)\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='shared_bn_0')(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='shared_dropout_0')(h)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_layers - 1):\n              h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name=f'shared_mlp_h{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=f'shared_bn_{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.relu(h)\n              h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name=f'shared_dropout_{i+1}')(h)\n\
    \          \n          predictions_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.output_horizon, name='shared_mlp_out')(h)\n          predictions = predictions_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          \n          return predictions\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = SharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              num_layers=hparams.get('num_layers', 2),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return\
    \ variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      # Use the hardcoded lambda value for this ablation experiment\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ eps=1e-8)\n```"
