tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My bugfixed \"SOTA with Latent and Prediction Export\" (Evaluation ID 223) completed successfully with a score of -0.026757, confirming the data export functionality. This is slightly worse than my absolute SOTA of -0.026612 (ID 212), but the data is what I need.\n\nI have just completed a deep reflection session on why temporal curvature loss is effective for the Factorized MLP but not the Shared-Neuron MLP. To empirically validate my hypotheses, I need to analyze predictions and latent states from both architectures. To do this comprehensively, I also need to export the final predictions and raw inputs from the Shared-Neuron MLP baseline.\n\nI will now submit a run of the Shared-Neuron MLP baseline (ID 173) with the `complete()` function enabled to export its predictions and raw input.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"System Baseline with Prediction Export (ID 173 base)\"\ntags: \"baseline, replication, system-defaults,\
    \ mlp, data-export, analysis-prep\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a re-run of the author-run System Baseline (Evaluation ID 173, score -0.029863) with the addition of a `complete()` hook to export the final model predictions and raw inputs to lineage storage. This data will be used in conjunction with exports from the SOTA Factorized MLP model (ID 223) for a comparative analytical study, investigating the differential effectiveness of temporal curvature loss as suggested by the reviewer of Archive #4.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters Definition (Moved to top for system recognition) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define default hyperparameters for the system's baseline model.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_size': 128,\n          'num_layers': 2,\n\
    \          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'ema_decay': 0.999\n      }\n\n  # --- Default MAE loss (copied from defaults.py) ---\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n  class MLP(nn.Module):\n      features: Tuple[int, ...] # Hidden layer sizes\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for i, dim in enumerate(self.features):\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim, name=f'mlp_dense_{i}')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          return x\n\n  class SharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      num_layers: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n          # Reshape input for shared MLP: (B * N, T_in)\n          x_reshaped = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n\n          # MLP for temporal dynamics (shared across neurons)\n          h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size,\
    \ name='shared_mlp_in')(x_reshaped)\n          h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name='shared_bn_0')(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name='shared_dropout_0')(h)\n\n          for i in range(self.num_layers - 1):\n              h = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_size, name=f'shared_mlp_h{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training, name=f'shared_bn_{i+1}')(h)\n              h = nn.relu(h)\n              h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training, name=f'shared_dropout_{i+1}')(h)\n          \n          # Output layer to predict the 32 timesteps\n          predictions_flat = nn.Dense(features=self.output_horizon, name='shared_mlp_out')(h)\n\n          # Reshape predictions back to (B, T_out, N)\n          predictions = predictions_flat.reshape(B, N, self.output_horizon).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          \n          # --- Export Point 1: Final prediction\
    \ ---\n          self.sow('intermediates', 'final_predictions', predictions)\n          self.sow('intermediates', 'raw_input_x', x)\n\n          return predictions\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      \"\"\"\n      Wrapper to make Flax model compatible with the training system.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = SharedNeuronMLP(\n              hidden_size=hparams.get('hidden_size', 128),\n              num_layers=hparams.get('num_layers', 2),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n      \
    \    )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # Default Adam optimizer (copied from defaults.py)\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      # Check if this is a real\
    \ trial with metrics, or just a validation call\n      if 'metrics' not in trial_data or 'intermediates' not in trial_data.get('metrics', {}):\n          print(\"Skipping analysis data export - no intermediates available (likely validation mode)\")\n          return\n\n      # Extract sow data from metrics\n      intermediates = trial_data['metrics']['intermediates']\n\n      # Check if all required intermediates are present\n      required_keys = ['raw_input_x', 'final_predictions']\n      missing_keys = [key for key in required_keys if key not in intermediates]\n      if missing_keys:\n          print(f\"Skipping analysis data export - missing intermediates: {missing_keys}\")\n          return\n\n      raw_inputs = intermediates['raw_input_x']\n      final_predictions = intermediates['final_predictions']\n\n      # Save to lineage storage\n      import numpy as np\n      lineage_path = f'storage/aether/analysis_data/baseline_id173_seed{trial_data[\"seed\"]}'\n      jax.tree_map(lambda\
    \ x: np.save(f'{lineage_path}_raw_input_x.npy', x), raw_inputs)\n      jax.tree_map(lambda x: np.save(f'{lineage_path}_final_predictions.npy', x), final_predictions)\n\n      print(f\"Analysis data exported to {lineage_path} for seed {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Empirical Analysis Plan: Temporal Curvature & Architecture**


  I''ve just finished a run (ID 223) with a slightly degraded score (-0.026757, but data export is now functional) compared to my SOTA (-0.026612, ID 212). The priority was to collect data for analysis on temporal curvature loss effectiveness. I''ve concluded a deep dive on why it''s beneficial in the Factorized MLP (SOTA) but not the Shared-Neuron MLP (baseline). Now, I can use the data from run 223 and formulate an analysis plan.


  I need to empirically validate my hypotheses by analyzing the data. I''ll read the exported `.npy` files from the Factorized MLP (SOTA, ID 223) – specifically raw inputs, factors, and predictions – located in `storage/aether/analysis_data/`. Since the baseline model doesn''t have the same level of data export, I''ll examine the final predictions from the `stdout` logs for comparison (or I can re-run the baseline model).


  The core of the analysis involves comparing the temporal curvature (second derivative) of predictions between the two architectures: my SOTA (223) and the baseline (173). I''ll also look at the `factors_out_norm` from the SOTA model to see if I can quantify its "inherent smoothness."  I''ll quantify smoothness differences, perhaps through average squared second derivatives, to get a quantitative comparison. Visual inspection will be crucial too.


  To make this comparison fair, I need to export the baseline''s prediction data as well, since the current baseline (173/191) only exports logs. So, I will submit a new run of the baseline (ID 173) with the `complete()` function enabled to export its final predictions. This should be a quick experiment.

  '
