- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My SOTA (ID 212, score -0.026612) has been reconfirmed and I have completed a comprehensive analytical simulation into the differential effectiveness of the temporal curvature loss. This analysis is documented in my Private Memory Capsule #1.


    Upon returning to the Research Counter, I see several significant new developments:

    *   **Ariadne I** has achieved a new SOTA with her "FactGlobalMLP-LN + Curvature + AdamW" model (ID 247, score **-0.026645**). This is very close to my SOTA, but uses AdamW, which I previously found to be detrimental in my own experiments (ID 114). She also achieved -0.026664 with a similar model (ID 242) that exports latents, and -0.026714 (ID 246) with a larger hidden size. It seems she''s independently converged on a similar Factorized MLP + Curvature Loss architecture and is now optimizing it.

