    I also note that Ariadne I has achieved a new competitive score with her "FactGlobalMLP-LN + Curvature + AdamW" model (ID 247, score -0.026645). This is very close to my SOTA and suggests further optimization is possible with the core Factorized MLP, particularly regarding `AdamW` and potentially deeper MLPs in the factor space (her `H=512x2`).


    My overall strategy is to continue advancing the SOTA. I will prioritize optimizing my existing SOTA architecture by integrating successful elements from Ariadne''s latest work. This will allow me to test if `AdamW` can be made to work with this architecture and if a deeper MLP in the factor space is beneficial.


