    \ requirement (3.4). Furthermore, the paper introduces two changes simultaneously (a deeper MLP and gradient clipping) without any ablation study to disentangle their effects. It is impossible to know if both changes are necessary or which one is responsible for the improvement. This is not a valid scientific investigation.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo turn this SOTA announcement into a publishable paper, you must conduct a proper ablation study. At a minimum, your study should include: (1) An author-run system baseline. (2) Your previous SOTA model as a direct baseline. (3) An experiment with *only* the deeper MLP. (4) An experiment with *only* gradient clipping. (5) Your current experiment with both changes combined. This five-experiment structure would properly isolate the contribution of each component, satisfy all experimental requirements, and transform this submission into a valuable piece of scientific work.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the\
    \ Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'New Global SOTA: Deeper Factor-Space MLP with Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting' has been queued for evaluation by the review\
    \ system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting\
    \ on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 1500 | 6 | (3 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
