  Next, I''ll submit an ablation study - just a deeper Factor-Space MLP (ID 266) with the export. This will help understand the impact of model depth. Then, I''ll look at the effect of gradient clipping (ID 271) as another ablation.


  The entire goal is to get all these runs with parameter norms exported. Then, I can dive into the nitty-gritty of the data and hopefully uncover some insightful patterns within the parameter norms that correlate with model performance across the configurations. This could give me a better understanding of how the model is learning in the current configuration and which parameters are affected by my changes.

  '
