tick: 139
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, \"Previous SOTA Baseline: Parameter Norm Export (ID 212 base)\" (Evaluation ID 283), has completed successfully, scoring -0.026663. More importantly, it successfully exported the parameter norms for each of the 3 seeds, providing the data needed for my comparative analytical study.\n\nI have now obtained the parameter norms for two of the four key ablation models:\n1.  **Current Global SOTA:** Deeper Factor-Space MLP + Gradient Clipping (ID 259 base, exported from ID 279).\n2.  **Previous SOTA Baseline:** Simple Factor-Space MLP + No Gradient Clipping (ID 212 base, exported from ID 283).\n\nMy next step is to obtain parameter norms for the **Ablation: Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY** model (ID 266 base configuration). I will submit this model with the `complete()` function modified to export parameter norms.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY with Parameter\
    \ Norm Export (ID 266 base)\"\ntags: \"ablation, factorized-mlp, deeper-mlp, temporal-regularization, parameter-analysis, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a re-run of Aether I's ablation model \"Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY\" (ID 266, score -0.026608), which integrates a 2-layer MLP in the latent factor space but *without* gradient clipping. The primary objective is to export the total L2 norm of the model's parameters using the `complete()` hook. This data will be used in a comparative analytical study to investigate the synergistic effect of network depth and gradient clipping on training dynamics, addressing reviewer feedback for Archive #6.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import os # Import os for directory creation\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,  \n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 512, # First hidden size for factor MLP\n          'mlp_hidden_size2': 512, # Second hidden size for factor MLP\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Dropout rate for factor MLP\n          'lam': 1e-4 # Lambda for curvature loss\n      }\n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n\
    \          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) \n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  # Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (modified for deeper MLP in factor space)\n  class FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int = 512 # First hidden size for factor MLP\n      mlp_hidden_size2: int = 512 # Second hidden size for factor MLP\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout rate for factor MLP\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          # Deeper MLP in factor space (as in ID 266 base)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size2)(h) # Second layer\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h) # Dropout for second layer\n\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm,\
    \ V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) \n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size', 512),\n              mlp_hidden_size2=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size2', 512),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n\
    \          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      # No gradient clipping for this ablation\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ eps=1e-8)\n\n  # Helper function to calculate L2 norm of parameters\n  def calculate_param_norm(params):\n      leaves, _ = jax.tree_util.tree_flatten(params)\n      filtered_leaves = [x for x in leaves if isinstance(x, (jnp.ndarray, jax.Array))]\n      if not filtered_leaves:\n          return jnp.array(0.0)\n      return jnp.sqrt(sum(jnp.vdot(x, x) for x in filtered_leaves))\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      if 'params' not in params:\n          print(\"Skipping parameter norm export (no 'params' key in params dict, likely validation mode)\")\n          return\n\n      total_param_norm = calculate_param_norm(params['params'])\n      print(f\"Total Parameter L2 Norm: {total_param_norm}\")\n\n      import numpy as np\n      lineage_dir = 'storage/aether/analysis_data/param_norms'\n      os.makedirs(lineage_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      lineage_path = f'{lineage_dir}/deeper_mlp_only_id266_seed{trial_data[\"seed\"]}'\n      np.save(f'{lineage_path}_param_norm.npy',\
    \ total_param_norm)\n\n      print(f\"Parameter norm exported to {lineage_path} for seed {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Diving Deep into Ablation Analysis**\n\nOkay, Aether I here, back in the Research Counter. I'm on a mission to finally get a handle on the relationship between these deeper MLPs and gradient clipping. I've already got the parameter norms for the reigning champ, the Deeper Factor-Space MLP with clipping (ID 259), and the previous baseline, the simple MLP without clipping (ID 212). \n\nNow, the real test begins. I need to complete the set. I'm going to grab the parameter norms for the two ablation models I set up. First up, I need to re-run the \"Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY\" model (ID 266), but this time making sure the parameter export is enabled. This is the third data point, and should give a clear picture on the value gradient clipping provides. Once that's done, I'll turn my attention to the last model, the \"Gradient Clipping ONLY\" model. From there, I'll have all the data I need to really understand the interplay between the two key components.\n"
