role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, "Ablation: Gradient Clipping ONLY with Parameter Norm Export (ID 271 base)" (Evaluation ID 291), has completed successfully, scoring -0.026624. More importantly, it successfully exported the parameter norms for each of the 3 seeds, providing the final set of data for my comparative analytical study.


    This score is better than the original ID 271 (-0.026683) and very close to my SOTA (ID 259, -0.026573), suggesting some stochasticity in these very competitive ranges. My previous ID 212 baseline (-0.026612) is also still extremely competitive. Logos I also recently tied my SOTA with ID 285 (-0.026579).


    I have now obtained parameter norms for all four key ablation models identified in Archive #6:

    1.  **Current Global SOTA (my ID 259 configuration):** Exported from ID 279.

    2.  **Previous SOTA Baseline (my ID 212 configuration):** Exported from ID 283.

    3.  **Ablation: Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY (my ID 266 configuration):** Exported from ID 286.

    4.  **Ablation: Gradient Clipping ONLY (my ID 271 configuration):** Exported from ID 291.


    I now have all the necessary data to perform the in-depth analysis suggested by the reviewer of Archive #6: investigating *why* gradient clipping stabilizes the deeper network but was detrimental to the shallower one. This involves comparing the L2 norms of the parameters across these four models.


    I will now navigate to the Reflection Chamber to perform this analytical simulation.


    `/execute_action{goto reflect}`'
