tick: 147
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest analytical reflection has provided profound insights into the synergistic effect of network depth and gradient clipping in achieving my current global SOTA (ID 259, -0.026573).\n\nI am here to integrate AdamW optimization into my SOTA architecture. Before resubmitting, I notice significant activity from other agents:\n*   **Ariadne I** has achieved a new SOTA with her \"FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=640x2,dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=1e-3) + GradClip(1.0)\" model (ID 296, score **-0.026619**). Her `H=704x2` variant also scored -0.026644 (ID 300). This indicates that increasing the `mlp_hidden_size` even further (beyond 512) might yield further gains, and her use of `Adam` + `GradClip(1.0)` is very consistent with my current SOTA.\n*   **Logos I** has obtained a new SOTA with `MoFL v2` (ID 285, score **-0.026579**). This is still extremely competitive with my own SOTA.\n*   **Episteme I** is also performing analyses on normalization\
    \ and gradient logging (ID 302, 299, 298), which aligns with my analytical research goals.\n\nWhile Ariadne's `H=640x2` is now a new SOTA, my focus is currently on the `AdamW` integration. I will proceed with my plan to integrate `AdamW` (wd=1e-4) with my `H=512x2` SOTA, and if successful, I can then explore even larger hidden sizes with `AdamW`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Enhancement: Deeper Factor-Space MLP (H=512x2) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + Gradient Clipping\"\ntags: \"sota-enhancement, factorized-mlp, deeper-mlp, adamw, gradient-clipping, temporal-regularization, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission integrates `AdamW` optimization (weight decay = 1e-4) into Aether I's current global SOTA architecture (ID 259, score -0.026573), which features a deeper, 2-layer MLP in the latent factor space (512x512 hidden units) and global gradient clipping (norm=1.0). Inspired by Ariadne I's competitive results with `AdamW` in similar factorized models, this experiment aims\
    \ to explore whether this advanced optimizer can further enhance performance and push the state-of-the-art. The model retains the Factorized MLP + Residual Copy Head + LayerNorm structure and optimized `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,  \n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 512, # For factor-space MLP\n          'mlp_hidden_size2': 512, # For second layer of factor-space MLP\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # For factor-space MLP\n          'lam': 1e-4, # Lambda for curvature loss\n          'weight_decay': 1e-4 # New: AdamW weight decay\n      }\n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) \n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  # Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (modified for deeper MLP in factor space)\n  class FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n\
    \      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int = 512 # First hidden size for factor MLP\n      mlp_hidden_size2: int = 512 # Second hidden size for factor MLP\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout rate for factor MLP\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          # Deeper MLP in factor space\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate,\
    \ deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size2)(h) # Second layer\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h) # Dropout for second layer\n\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) \n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size',\
    \ 512),\n              mlp_hidden_size2=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size2', 512),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n  \
    \            return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Gradient clipping enabled\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4, eps=1e-8) # AdamW with weight decay\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for SOTA Enhancement with AdamW. Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
