    \ ~283.47)\n  2.  **Previous SOTA Baseline:** Simple Factor-Space MLP + No Gradient Clipping (ID 212 config, data from ID 283: Avg Param Norm ~180.3)\n  3.  **Ablation: Deeper Factor-Space MLP ONLY:** Deeper Factor-Space MLP + No Gradient Clipping (ID 266 config, data from ID 286: Avg Param Norm ~194.4)\n  4.  **Ablation: Gradient Clipping ONLY:** Simple Factor-Space MLP + Gradient Clipping (ID 271 config, data from ID 314: Avg Param Norm ~208.17)\n\n  The goal is to explain the synergistic effect of network depth and gradient clipping, and why gradient clipping alone was detrimental to the shallower network.\n\n  Specifically, in this first tick:\n  1.  **Data Recap and Initial Observations:** Present the collected scores and average parameter L2 norms for each of the four configurations.\n  2.  **Direct Comparisons:** Make initial direct comparisons of scores and norms between pairs of models to highlight immediate effects (e.g., Previous SOTA vs. Deeper MLP Only, Previous SOTA vs.\
    \ Clipping Only).\ntick: 3\n```"
