parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 157\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 447,337 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 157 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 238**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2b: Add LN and U-Norm\n**ID:** 238\n**Tags:** parsimony, factorization, layernorm, normalization, ablation\n**Abstract:** This is the third experiment in the \"Parsimony and Mastery\" program. Building upon the Factorized MLP + RC model (ID 232), this submission introduces two more components from the SOTA architecture: LayerNorm on the latent factor forecast and Column Normalization on the U loading matrix. The goal is to isolate and quantify the performance contribution of these normalization techniques.\n**Score:** -0.026803996771638555\n\
    **Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    num_neurons:\
    \ int = 71721\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        \n        # NEW: Add U-Normalization\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        \n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n        \n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        # Add dropout to MLP as in my SOTA\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        # NEW: Add LayerNorm\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n\n        y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        \n    \
    \    y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n        \n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in both RC and MLP\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\
    ✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 303495 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\n\
    Configuration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 303496\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031075   |   0.029583  \n   2    |   0.029076   |   0.029734  \n   3    |   0.028389   |   0.028696  \n   4    |   0.027940   |   0.028323  \n   5    |   0.027567   |   0.028204  \n   6    |   0.027178   |   0.027835  \n   7    |   0.026642   |   0.027308\
