tick: 157
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest analytical reflection has provided profound insights into the synergistic effect of network depth and gradient clipping in achieving my current global SOTA (ID 259, -0.026573). I have updated Archive #6 with these findings.\n\nI have just reviewed Episteme I's Archive #7, which systematically reconstructs the Factorized Forecaster and highlights the **paramount importance of normalization techniques**. I have also reviewed her \"Model C: + Normalization\" (ID 238) code. Her LayerNorm and U-Normalization implementation are consistent with my SOTA. This reinforces my understanding that stable optimization is key.\n\nMy focus now shifts to further optimizing my SOTA (ID 259) by exploring strategies suggested by my analysis and other agents. Logos I has achieved a new SOTA with her \"MoFL with Latent-Space Gating\" (ID 320, score **-0.026614**). This is extremely competitive and uses a different gating mechanism than my architecture.\
    \ More importantly, Ariadne I has achieved a new Global SOTA with her `FactGlobalMLP-LN (k=320,p=32,H=768x2,dr=0.10) + Adam(lr=9e-4) + GradClip(1.0)` model (ID 306, score **-0.026608**). Even more recently, she achieved -0.026619 with ID 296 (`H=640x2`) and **-0.026608 with ID 306 (`H=768x2`)**. This is extremely competitive and suggests that my `H=512x2` might not be the optimal deeper MLP size.\n\nMy next research step is to **update my SOTA architecture to use a larger hidden size in the factor-space MLP**, specifically Ariadne's `H=768x2` configuration. I will keep my existing Adam optimizer with gradient clipping and `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss, as these components have been rigorously validated.\n\n**Experiment Plan:**\n1.  **Modify `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN`:** Update `mlp_hidden_size` and `mlp_hidden_size2` from `512` to `768`.\n2.  **Retain Architecture/Optimization:** My current global SOTA architecture (Deeper Factor-Space MLP with gradient clipping, Residual Copy Head,\
    \ LayerNorm, Curvature Loss).\n\nThis experiment aims to push the SOTA further by optimizing the network depth based on competitive results.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Enhancement: Deeper Factor-Space MLP (H=768x2) + Gradient Clipping\"\ntags: \"sota-enhancement, factorized-mlp, deeper-mlp, hidden-size-tuning, gradient-clipping, temporal-regularization, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission further enhances Aether I's current global SOTA Factorized MLP architecture (ID 259, score -0.026573) by increasing the hidden size of the deeper MLP within the latent factor space from `512x2` to `768x2`. This optimization is inspired by Ariadne I's competitive results with larger hidden sizes (e.g., ID 306, score -0.026608). The model retains global gradient clipping (norm=1.0) and the optimized `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss, aiming to push the state-of-the-art further by maximizing the expressive power of the deeper network.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as\
    \ nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,  \n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 768, # Increased hidden size for factor MLP (NEW)\n          'mlp_hidden_size2': 768, # Increased second hidden size for factor MLP (NEW)\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # For factor-space MLP\n          'lam': 1e-4 # Lambda for curvature loss\n      }\n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead\n  class\
    \ ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) \n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          final_output = output + residual\n          return final_output\n\n  # Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (modified for deeper MLP in factor space)\n  class FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int # First hidden size for factor MLP\n      mlp_hidden_size2: int # Second hidden size for factor MLP\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # Dropout rate for factor MLP\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def\
    \ __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k = self.rank_k\n          p = self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          # Deeper MLP in factor space with increased hidden size\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h)\n          \n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size2)(h) # Second layer\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(h) # Dropout for second layer\n\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon\
    \ * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) \n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size', 768),\n              mlp_hidden_size2=hparams.get('mlp_hidden_size2', 768),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n          self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats']\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions,\
    \ targets, params, x):\n      return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Gradient clipping enabled\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8) # Adam optimizer\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for SOTA Enhancement with H=768x2. Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
