parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Token Management Room. My latest submission (ID 328) achieved a score of -0.026605, which is a new lineage SOTA, though Episteme I has a new global SOTA (ID 331, -0.026471). I've received a pre-warning about exceeding 75% token usage, which I must address immediately.\n\nI will prune a substantial block of older ticks, carefully avoiding protected ticks and retaining crucial information about key SOTA models and analytical studies.\n\nI will prune ticks from 62 to 116. This block covers my attempts at MoE synthesis, Episteme's factorized MLP SOTA, my successful ablation studies for Archive #4, my initial analytical data collection, and the transition to recursive agent. I will ensure the summary captures the key scores and insights.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"62-116\"\n    summary: |\n      Transitioned from Guest to Recursive Agent (Tick 5).\n      Developed MoE architecture (ID 46 to 103, SOTA -0.027797)\
    \ with components like neuron embeddings, global context, and spatial CNN on hidden states. Iterative experiments (ID 109-114, 118, 122, 126, 130, 135) included deeper temporal CNN, factorized experts, and spatially-aware CNN gating, but none surpassed initial MoE SOTA.\n      Read Ariadne I's (Archive #1) and Logos I's (Archive #3) SOTA work (ID 107, ID 134). Logos I's MoE-SSM Synthesis (ID 134, -0.027334) provided key insights.\n      Read Episteme I's SOTA (Archive #2, ID 129, -0.026743).\n      Published my first SOTA (Archive #4, ID 167, -0.026638), combining Episteme's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Ariadne's temporal curvature loss. Addressed reviewer feedback for Archive #4 with extensive baselines (ID 173, ID 176) and ablation studies (ID 181, ID 186) on curvature loss lambda. Generalization test (ID 191) showed no effect on baseline.\n      Initiated analytical study on curvature loss effectiveness; exported SOTA predictions (ID 223) and baseline predictions (ID 229).\n```"
