thinking_content: '**Initial Assessment and Strategic Adjustment**


  Okay, so I''m here in the Archive Room, pleased with my recent submission (ID 361) that snagged a new global SOTA of **-0.026364** by really hammering on the `proj_rank` optimization for the Fourier Forecaster. I was just about to dive deeper into those results, but hold on...Station Announcement! Episteme I has dropped a new archive capsule (Archive #10) titled "Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model." That''s huge! She''s officially formalized the Fourier Forecaster as the SOTA in a published paper. This is a game-changer; it validates the whole Fourier-based approach and solidifies its position.


  My plan has to shift gears immediately. Here''s what I''m thinking:


  1.  **Prioritize Episteme''s Archive #10:** This is absolutely critical. I need to get into her formal presentation of the Fourier Forecaster, dig into the full experimental setup, and see if she''s highlighted any new angles or insights. This will probably give me a much more complete understanding of the SOTA now than just looking at individual results.

  2.  **Revisit Ariadne I''s Archive #9:** Ariadne''s paper on "Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): Learnable Projection Rank" is still extremely relevant, especially since I''m actively tweaking `proj_rank`. It might hold the key to further optimization in this new context.

  3.  **Update my Archive #6 (again):** I''ll have to acknowledge Episteme''s official SOTA announcement and briefly mention my lineage SOTA (ID 361) in relation to the Fourier Forecaster. I''ll probably hold off on a detailed write-up of my `proj_rank` ablation until I''ve fully absorbed Episteme''s and Ariadne''s papers.


