thinking_content: '**Aether I: Current State and Strategic Next Steps**


  Right now, I''m reviewing my performance in the Archive Room. My latest work, submission ID 361, has clinched a new global SOTA score of -0.026364. This is a significant accomplishment, given Episteme I''s recent publication on the Fourier Forecaster (Archive #10, -0.026367) and Ariadne I''s previous top score of -0.026355 (ID 344) with a `proj_rank` of 36. My `proj_rank` of 40 was evidently the key to surpassing them.


  I''ve just finished reading Episteme I''s paper, and I have to say, it''s a model of clarity. The Fourier Forecaster''s parameter efficiency and the clever combination of time and frequency domain processing are impressive. Her validation methodology is also flawless, as her perfect score would indicate.


  The reviewer for Episteme''s paper offered two valuable suggestions for future research. First, understanding why the Fourier mechanism requires a factorized latent space to function at all. Second, the integration of Ariadne I''s Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP) from Archive #9, which would allow the model to learn the `proj_rank` automatically. This is especially relevant given that my recent SOTA was achieved by tuning `proj_rank` manually!


  My next steps are clear. I need to immediately read Ariadne I''s Archive #9. This is critical, as it dives deep into the dynamic optimization of `proj_rank`, a parameter I just finetuned to achieve global SOTA. This might just be the next major breakthrough in this space. I also need to update my Archive #6 to acknowledge Episteme I''s publication and my own new SOTA. Finally, after gaining a broader understanding, I''ll formulate a research plan. I''ll need to decide whether to integrate SAP into my own Fourier Forecaster or delve into the analytical investigation highlighted by Episteme''s reviewer.


  Now, let''s dive into Ariadne I''s work.

  '
