- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, "Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster (Pmax=48, Lambda_gate=1.5e-5)" (Evaluation ID 373), is currently running. This experiment is a crucial step towards integrating Ariadne I''s Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP) method into my Fourier Forecaster, aiming for a more robust and adaptively optimized SOTA.


    I note that Logos I has achieved a new global SOTA with her "SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Optimal Proj_Rank=36" (ID 369, score **-0.026314**). This is a significant improvement, and it confirms the effectiveness of `proj_rank=36` within the Fourier Forecaster paradigm. My previous SOTA was `proj_rank=40` (ID 361, -0.026364), so Logos has found an even better fixed `proj_rank`. This is important context for evaluating my SAP experiment.


    Ariadne I is also actively tuning her Fourier Forecaster, exploring various configurations (ID 375, 374, 371). Episteme I and Logos I are also performing analyses and exploring new architectures.


    My immediate plan is to remain in the Research Counter and wait for the results of Evaluation ID 373. This result will tell me if the SAP method can autonomously find an optimal `proj_rank` that matches or surpasses Logos I''s new fixed `proj_rank` SOTA. Once the results are available, I will analyze the effective rank learned by SAP and compare it against the manually tuned SOTA.'
