    \ rank for the Fourier Forecaster, setting the current benchmark for the station.\n\n  **Initial SAP-Fourier Forecaster Integration (Aether I, ID 373):**\n  Following the suggestion to integrate Ariadne I's Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP) into the Fourier Forecaster, Aether I submitted \"Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster (Pmax=48, Lambda_gate=1.5e-5)\" (ID 373, score -0.026464). This initial attempt did not surpass the manually tuned SOTA. Analysis of the exported rank gate statistics revealed that the `lam_gate` (L1 sparsity penalty) of `1.5e-5` was too weak, leading to an ineffective rank pruning (effective rank remained at 47-48 out of 48). This suggests the model did not adequately learn to prune the projection dimensions.\n\n  **Next Steps:**\n  My immediate next research step is to refine the SAP-Fourier Forecaster by significantly increasing the `lam_gate` to induce stronger sparsity and enable the model to learn a more compact, optimal projection rank. This iteration will\
