tick: 194
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 194\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 319,370 / 600,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 194 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Logos I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 369, Proj_Rank=36)' (ID: 400) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026272441653875253\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 400\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError in Flax module that was preventing initialization. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) attempted\
    \ to access `self.parent.hparams` within nested Flax modules (`ResidualCopyHead` and `FourierForecasterLN`). This is invalid because:\n\n1. Flax modules don't have a `parent` attribute that provides access to outer class attributes\n2. The `hparams` dictionary exists in the `ModelWrapper` class, not in the Flax module scope\n3. This caused an `AttributeError: 'Scope' object has no attribute 'hparams'` during model initialization\n\nThe error occurred at three locations:\n- Line 19: `nn.Dropout(rate=self.parent.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1))` in `ResidualCopyHead`\n- Line 40: `nn.Dropout(rate=self.parent.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1))` in `FourierForecasterLN`\n- Line 42: `nn.Dropout(rate=self.parent.hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1))` in `FourierForecasterLN`\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified both Flax modules to accept `dropout_rate` as a proper module attribute:\n\n1. **ResidualCopyHead**: Added `dropout_rate: float = 0.1` as a class attribute\n2. **FourierForecasterLN**: Added `dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.1` as a class attribute\n3. **ModelWrapper**: Pass the dropout rate when instantiating the model:\n   ```python\n   self.model = FourierForecasterLN(\n       rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n       proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n       dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']  # Added this\n   )\n   ```\n4. **ResidualCopyHead instantiation**: Pass dropout rate from parent module:\n   ```python\n   y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, training=training)\n   ```\n\nThis follows the standard Flax pattern where module parameters are defined as class attributes and passed during initialization, rather than attempting to access outer scope variables.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The fix maintains the same functionality while using proper Flax module architecture\n- All dropout rates remain configurable via the hyperparameters dictionary\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot\
    \ modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- Hyperparameters Definition ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36, # Fixed proj_rank as per Logos I's SOTA\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1 # Dropout rate for MLPs (standard)\n    }\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n# Episteme's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/episteme/fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py)\n\
    class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\n# Episteme's FourierForecasterLN (adapted from storage/episteme/fourier_forecaster_v2_ln.py)\nclass FourierForecasterLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int # Fixed projection rank\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    num_neurons: int = 71721\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n\
    \        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # --- Fourier Branch ---\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1) # RFFT on temporal dimension\n        x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, N, T_in_freq)\n\n        # Project into factor space in frequency domain\n        factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T # (B, T_in_freq, k)\n\n        # Flatten real and imaginary parts for MLP\n        factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n\n        # Deeper MLP in flattened factor-frequency space (H=512x2 from previous SOTA)\n        # Note: Original Episteme code for FourierForecasterLN uses H=512x2.\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_in_flat);\
    \ h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h) # Output 2*k for real/imag\n\n        # Reshape and split into real and imaginary parts\n        factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B, num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n        factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1) # Reconstruct complex\n\n        # Add LayerNorm in the frequency domain (separately for real and imag)\n        norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n        norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n        factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n        # Decode from frequency-domain factors back to neuron space\n      \
    \  y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T # (B, T_out_freq, N)\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1) # IFFT to time domain\n\n        # --- Time Branch ---\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, training=training)\n\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n# --- Submission API ---\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in ResidualCopyHead and MLP\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\
    \n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Uses temporal curvature loss\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), # Uses gradient clipping\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"Completion for Fourier Forecaster Replication of Logos I's SOTA. Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\nCompletion for Fourier Forecaster Replication of Logos I's SOTA. Seed: 42\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting\
