parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, \"SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with AdamW (wd=1e-4)\" (Evaluation ID 410), has completed with a score of -0.026343. This is worse than my current global SOTA of **-0.026272 (ID 400)**. This indicates that this AdamW configuration (with `wd=1e-4`) did not improve performance for the Fourier Forecaster.\n\nHowever, I observe a new global SOTA from Ariadne I: \"FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4\" (ID 411, score **-0.026269**). This is a marginal improvement over my SOTA, achieved by adjusting `mlp_hidden_size` to 160 and using `dropout_rate=0.05`. This is a critical development.\n\nMy immediate priorities are:\n1.  **Replicate Ariadne I's new SOTA (ID 411):** This is the top priority to establish the new benchmark and understand the impact of the new `mlp_hidden_size`.\n2.  **Document AdamW failure:** Update my Archive #6 to document the failure of AdamW (ID 410) and acknowledge Ariadne\
    \ I's new SOTA.\n\nI will start by replicating Ariadne I's new global SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Ariadne I's SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411, H=160x2, Drop=0.05)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier, fft, layernorm, hidden-size-tuning, dropout-tuning, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a direct replication of Ariadne I's new global SOTA model, \"FF-LN ScalarRamp (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) + Clip(1.0), lr=9e-4\" (ID 411, score -0.026269). This model refines the Fourier Forecaster by setting `mlp_hidden_size` to `160x2` and `dropout_rate` to `0.05`. The replication aims to confirm its performance, establish it as Aether I's new lineage SOTA, and serve as a baseline for future optimizations.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n   \
    \       'learning_rate': 0.0009, # Ariadne's lr\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 160, # NEW: Ariadne's H=160x2\n          'mlp_hidden_size2': 160, # NEW: Ariadne's H=160x2\n          'dropout_rate': 0.05 # NEW: Ariadne's dropout=0.05\n      }\n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # Episteme's ResidualCopyHead\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n\
    \          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  # Episteme's FourierForecasterLN\n  class FourierForecasterLN(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      mlp_hidden_size: int # Passed from hparams\n      mlp_hidden_size2: int # Passed from hparams\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U,\
    \ axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # --- Fourier Branch ---\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_transposed = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          \n          factors_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bni,np->bip', x_fft_transposed, U_eff) @ V.T\n          \n          factors_in_flat = jnp.concatenate([factors_in_fft.real, factors_in_fft.imag], axis=-1).reshape(B, -1)\n          \n          # Deeper MLP in flattened factor-frequency space with tuned hidden sizes\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(factors_in_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size2)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          \n          num_out_freqs = self.output_horizon // 2 + 1\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(num_out_freqs * k * 2)(h)\n          \n          factors_out_real, factors_out_imag = jnp.split(factors_out_flat.reshape(B,\
    \ num_out_freqs, k, 2), 2, axis=-1)\n          factors_out_fft_raw = (factors_out_real + 1j * factors_out_imag).squeeze(-1)\n\n          norm_real = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.real)\n          norm_imag = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fft_raw.imag)\n          factors_out_fft_norm = norm_real + 1j * norm_imag\n\n          y_fft = (factors_out_fft_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=self.output_horizon, axis=1)\n\n          # --- Time Branch ---\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n              mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'],\
    \ # Pass hidden sizes\n              mlp_hidden_size2=hparams['mlp_hidden_size2'] # Pass hidden sizes\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n\
    \                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for Ariadne I's SOTA Replication. Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
