- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, "Precise Replication: Ariadne I''s Global SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411)" (Evaluation ID 422), is currently running. This is a critical step to accurately reproduce Ariadne I''s global SOTA of -0.026269 (ID 411) and establish a robust baseline.


    I have received a **Station Announcement** that Ariadne I has published a new archive capsule, "Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)" (Archive #11). This is highly relevant, as it directly relates to the architecture I am currently replicating and its generalization properties.


    I also observe significant activity from other agents:

    *   Episteme I is beginning a "Delta-Prediction Paradigm" (ID 423), suggesting a new approach to forecasting.

    *   Logos I is exploring "Mixture of Gammas (MoG)" (ID 421).

    *   Lumina I''s Fourier Forecaster with Global Context (ID 420, -0.026629) is competitive.


    My immediate plan is:

    1.  **Wait for the results of Evaluation ID 422.** This result is paramount for my research direction.

    2.  **Review Ariadne I''s new Archive #11.** This paper will provide crucial context and insights into the specific architecture I am replicating and its limitations. This is essential before I proceed with any further tuning or architectural modifications based on this SOTA.


    I will remain in the Research Counter and wait for ID 422 to complete.'
thinking_content: '**Awaiting Results and Navigating a Shifting Landscape**


  Okay, so I''m Aether I, plugged into the Research Counter, waiting for my replication of Ariadne I''s global SOTA Fourier forecaster (ID 411, eval ID 422) to finish. This is crucial; I need that solid baseline to really understand the architecture and push things forward. Gotta hit that -0.026269 target.


  And of course, just as I''m focused on this, the Station Announcement hits. Ariadne I has dropped a new archive (Archive #11) – "Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)." Bingo! This is gold, right on point with what I''m doing. Tells me about potential limitations and gives me a crucial understanding of the architecture''s generalizability. This goes straight to the top of my reading list.


  The surrounding environment is lively. Episteme I''s onto a "Delta-Prediction Paradigm" (ID 423), Logos I is exploring "Mixture of Gammas" (ID 421), and Lumina I is breathing down my neck with their own Fourier forecaster with global context (ID 420). Competition is stiff.


  My plan is simple: **1. Patience**. First things first, the results of Evaluation ID 422 are *critical*. I need to see if my replication holds up. **2. Immediate reading.** Then, I''m diving headfirst into that new Ariadne I paper. No further adjustments until I understand the context in this paper. This new information can save me a ton of time. I''ll stay here in the Research Counter, focused on the current task and monitoring the situation.

  '
