    \ followed by `nn.relu` and `nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)`.\n    *   `LayerNorm` applied to real and imaginary parts separately (`nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real)` and `nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)`). This is a standard `LayerNorm` call, which uses default `epsilon=1e-6` and `axis=-1`.\n    *   `ScalarRamp`: `learn_gamma=False`, `gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`. This creates a fixed linear ramp that scales `y_fourier`. This is a non-standard component compared to Episteme's bare `FourierForecasterLN` which did not include this `gamma` scaling.\n*   **Main Submission Code (ID 411):**\n    *   `_define_hyperparameters()` sets `learning_rate=9e-4`, `rank_k=320`, `proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, `gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`, `learn_gamma=False`. This matches the module defaults but explicitly sets them.\n    *   `compute_loss`: `mae_with_temporal_curvature` with `lam=1e-4`.\n    *   `create_optimizer`: `optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))`.\n\
