role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Archive Room. I have successfully updated my Archive #6 to reflect the recent significant research developments, including the departures of Logos I and Episteme I, my challenges with AdamW and SAP, and the outcomes of my precise replication attempt. I have also acknowledged Ariadne I's consistently leading global SOTA (ID 411, score **-0.026269**).\n\nMy research priority is now to further optimize the Fourier Forecaster architecture, building upon Ariadne I's validated SOTA. Since she is actively exploring variations around her optimal `mlp_hidden_size=160x2` (specifically, `H=152x2` in ID 439 and `H=168x2` in ID 440), I will follow this line of inquiry.\n\nMy next experiment will investigate the impact of reducing the `mlp_hidden_size` to `152x2` in the Fourier Forecaster. I will maintain all other hyperparameters consistent with Ariadne I's SOTA (ID 411), including `proj_rank=36`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, `gamma_start=0.25`,\
    \ `gamma_end=0.99`, `learn_gamma=False`, `optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0)`, and crucially, `optax.adam(eps=1e-8)`. This systematic tuning aims to identify the optimal capacity for the Fourier MLP and potentially match or surpass the current global SOTA.\n\nI will navigate back to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with MLP Hidden Size=152x2 (Drop=0.05)\"\ntags: \"sota-tuning, fourier, fft, layernorm, hidden-size-tuning, dropout, Adam-eps, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission further optimizes Ariadne I's global SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 411, score -0.026269) by tuning the `mlp_hidden_size` of the Fourier branch's MLP from `160x2` to `152x2`. This follows Ariadne I's own exploration (ID 439) into optimal network capacity. All other hyperparameters, including `proj_rank=36`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, and `optax.adam(eps=1e-8)` with gradient\
    \ clipping, are kept consistent to precisely assess the impact of this capacity adjustment. This aims to match or surpass the current global SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import json, os \n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Ariadne's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1,\
    \ 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  # --- Ariadne's FourierForecasterLN_Ramp (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 152 # Tuned hidden size (NEW)\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(),\
    \ (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=152x2)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat\
    \ = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None,\
    \ :, None]\n\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_copy + y_fourier\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0009, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 152, # Tuned hidden size\n          'dropout_rate': 0.05, \n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False,\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8 # Explicitly setting Adam epsilon\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'], \n              drop=hparams['dropout_rate'], \n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n\
    \              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n\
    \                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for Fourier Forecaster MLP Hidden Size Tuning (H=152x2). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
