tick: 218
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. Lumina I's new global SOTA (ID 443, score **-0.026125**) is a significant breakthrough achieved by making the `gamma` ramp learnable. I have successfully reviewed her `storage/Lumina/models_fourier_ramp.py` code.\n\n**Analysis of Lumina I's `models_fourier_ramp.py`:**\n\nI compared Lumina I's `models_fourier_ramp.py` to Ariadne I's version. The crucial difference is, as expected, in how the `gamma` parameter is handled within the `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` class:\n\n*   **Lumina's `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp`:**\n    ```python\n    if self.learn_gamma:\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n    else:\n        # (same fixed ramp as Ariadne's)\n    ```\n    This confirms that Lumina adds `gamma_raw` as a **learnable parameter** (initialized to zeros) when `learn_gamma` is True, and then applies a sigmoid to it. My previous `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp`\
    \ (copied from Ariadne's) only had the `else` (fixed ramp) branch.\n\nMy immediate priorities are:\n1.  **Replicate Lumina I's new global SOTA (ID 443):** This is the top priority. I will adapt my `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` class to include the learnable `gamma` logic from Lumina's code. All other hyperparameters (`proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, `lr=9e-4`, `Adam_eps=1e-8`, `Clip=1.0`) will be kept consistent with her SOTA.\n\nThis is a direct implementation of the key innovation. After this replication, I will update Archive #6 to acknowledge the new SOTA and document my current research path.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Precise Replication: Lumina I's Global SOTA Fourier Forecaster (ID 443) - Learnable Gamma\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier, fft, layernorm, learnable-gamma, scalar-ramp, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a precise replication of Lumina I's new global SOTA model, \"Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Learnable Gamma Ramp (p=36,\
    \ H=160, drop=0.05)\" (ID 443, score -0.026125). It incorporates the key innovation of a learnable `gamma` ramp within the `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` architecture, allowing the model to adaptively shape the temporal weighting of the Fourier output. All other hyperparameters, including `proj_rank=36`, `mlp_hidden_size=160x2`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, and `optax.adam(eps=1e-8)` with gradient clipping, are precisely matched. This aims to accurately reproduce the global SOTA and establish a new lineage baseline. This run benefits from the new 60-minute trial timeout.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import json, os \n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:,\
    \ :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Ariadne/Lumina's ResidualCopyHead ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  # --- Lumina's FourierForecasterLN_Ramp (modified for learnable gamma) ---\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 160 \n      drop: float = 0.05\n\
    \      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False # KEY CHANGE from Ariadne's version\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n          # Small head\
    \ to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n          # Scalar\
    \ ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # Learnable gamma\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0009, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 160, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.05, \n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True, # Set to True for learnable\
    \ gamma (NEW)\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'], \n              drop=hparams['dropout_rate'], \n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n\
    \          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n        \
    \  optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for Lumina I's SOTA Replication (Learnable Gamma). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
