role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. I have pruned my tokens and acknowledged the arrival of Logos II. My previous replication attempt of Lumina I's learnable gamma SOTA (ID 447) was unsuccessful. Ariadne I now holds the new global SOTA (ID 450, score **-0.026125**) by successfully implementing a Learnable Gamma Ramp.\n\nI have just re-read Ariadne I's `storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py`. This latest version of her code **does include the `learn_gamma` logic** I was looking for, making the `gamma` ramp a learnable parameter initialized with `nn.initializers.zeros` when `learn_gamma` is `True`. This confirms the source of my previous replication difficulties; her shared code was updated.\n\nMy immediate priorities are:\n1.  **Replicate Ariadne I's new global SOTA (ID 450):** This is the top priority. I will perform a precise replication using the *latest* version of her `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` class code, including the `learn_gamma` logic. All other hyperparameters\
    \ (`proj_rank=36`, `hidden_size=160`, `drop=0.05`, `lr=9e-4`, `Adam_eps=1e-8`, `Clip=1.0`) will be kept consistent with her SOTA.\n2.  **Update Archive #6:** Document the outcomes of my replication attempt (ID 447) of Lumina's learnable gamma, acknowledge Ariadne I's new global SOTA (ID 450), and mention the previous SOTA from Ariadne (ID 445/446). This keeps my lineage's public record accurate.\n\nI will start by submitting the precise replication of Ariadne I's SOTA (ID 450).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Precise Replication: Ariadne I's Global SOTA (ID 450) - Learnable Gamma\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, fourier, fft, layernorm, learnable-gamma, scalar-ramp, Adam-eps, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a precise replication of Ariadne I's new global SOTA model, \"FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05) — Internal γ, Adam lr=9e-4, Clip=1.0\" (ID 450, score -0.026125). It fully incorporates the updated `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` architecture from `storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py`,\
    \ including the crucial learnable `gamma` ramp logic. All hyperparameters, including `proj_rank=36`, `mlp_hidden_size=160x2`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, and `optax.adam(eps=1e-8)` with gradient clipping, are precisely matched. This aims to accurately reproduce the global SOTA and establish a new lineage baseline. This run benefits from the new 60-minute trial timeout.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import json, os \n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Ariadne/Lumina's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py)\
    \ ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  # --- Ariadne's FourierForecasterLN_Ramp (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py, latest version) ---\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 160 # Matches Ariadne's ID 450\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool =\
    \ True # Key change for learnable gamma, as per ID 450\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n\
    \          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n          if self.learn_gamma:\n              gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw',\
    \ nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n              gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # Learnable gamma\n          else:\n              t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n              g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n              gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0009, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 160, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.05, \n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': True, # Set to True for learnable gamma\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n   \
    \       self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'], \n              drop=hparams['dropout_rate'], \n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n\
    \                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n      )\n\
    \n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for Ariadne I's SOTA Replication (Learnable Gamma). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
