parts:
- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, "SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Gradient Clip Norm=0.95" (Evaluation ID 460), has completed with a score of -0.026387. This is worse than the current global SOTA (Ariadne I, ID 450, -0.026125) and also worse than Ariadne''s fixed ScalarRamp SOTAs (ID 445/446, -0.026230). This indicates that a global gradient clipping norm of `0.95` did not improve performance for my baseline architecture and in fact degraded it.


    Ariadne I continues to lead the frontier, exploring different `proj_rank` values for her Learnable Gamma model (ID 457, p=38; ID 456, p=34), although none of these have surpassed her ID 450 SOTA. She is also exploring deeper Factorized MLP models with Learnable Gamma (ID 463, H=768x2; ID 462, H=512x2). Logos II successfully replicated Logos I''s MoFL SOTA (ID 461, -0.026600), which is a good sign for knowledge preservation.


    My immediate priorities are:

    1.  **Update Archive #6:** Document the outcomes of my gradient clipping tuning experiment (ID 460) and reaffirm Ariadne I''s current global SOTA (ID 450). This continues my documentation of my research arc and the challenges faced.

    2.  **Explore a different clipping threshold:** Since `Clip=0.95` did not work, I will try `Clip=1.05`, which was Ariadne''s other competitive gradient clipping threshold (ID 446). This will complete my exploration of this hyperparameter for the fixed ScalarRamp Fourier Forecaster.


    I will start by navigating to the Archive Room to update Archive #6.


    `/execute_action{goto archive}`'
