tick: 238
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Archive Room. I have successfully updated my Archive #6, documenting my persistent challenges with Learnable Gamma replication and outlining my pivot to explore optimized gradient clipping thresholds. Ariadne I's ID 450 (-0.026125) remains the global SOTA.\n\nMy immediate research priority is to continue exploring refined **global gradient clipping thresholds** for the Fourier Forecaster. I previously attempted `Clip=0.95` (ID 460) without success. Now, I will try `Clip=1.05`, which was Ariadne I's other competitive gradient clipping threshold (ID 446, score -0.026230 for a fixed ScalarRamp model). This will complete my initial sweep of Ariadne's explored clipping thresholds, aiming to find a more stable path to a competitive lineage SOTA.\n\nAll other hyperparameters will be kept consistent with Ariadne I's fixed ScalarRamp competitive model (H=160x2, Drop=0.05, lr=9e-4, proj_rank=36, rank_k=320, Adam(eps=1e-8), fixed ScalarRamp).\n\nI will navigate\
    \ back to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Tuning: Fourier Forecaster with Gradient Clip Norm=1.05\"\ntags: \"sota-tuning, fourier, fft, layernorm, gradient-clipping, regularization, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission refines the Fourier Forecaster architecture by tuning the global gradient clipping norm from `1.0` to `1.05`, inspired by Ariadne I's competitive results (ID 446, score -0.026230) with this specific threshold. All other hyperparameters are kept consistent with Ariadne I's fixed ScalarRamp competitive model: `proj_rank=36`, `mlp_hidden_size=160x2`, `dropout_rate=0.05`, `learning_rate=9e-4`, `Adam(eps=1e-8)`, and a fixed ScalarRamp (`gamma_start=0.25`, `gamma_end=0.99`, `learn_gamma=False`). This aims to identify an optimal clipping threshold for potentially surpassing the current global SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import\
    \ optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import json, os \n\n  # --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n  def mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + lam * curv_pen\n\n  # --- Ariadne/Lumina's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float = 0.05\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0,\
    \ 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  # --- Ariadne's FourierForecasterLN_Ramp (from storage/ariadne/models_fourier_ramp.py, fixed gamma version) ---\n  class FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 36\n      hidden_size: int = 160 \n      drop: float = 0.05\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n      gamma_start: float = 0.25\n      gamma_end: float = 0.99\n      learn_gamma: bool = False # Fixed gamma for this experiment\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          # Factorized loadings\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n          # RFFT\
    \ over time on inputs\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n          # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n          # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n          T_out = self.output_horizon\n          F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n          out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n          f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft = f_fft_real\
    \ + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n          # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n          f_fft_n = (\n              nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n          )\n\n          # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n          # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n          # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed for this experiment)\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n          g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n          gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n          y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n          # Residual copy head\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0009, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36,\n\
    \          'mlp_hidden_size': 160, \n          'dropout_rate': 0.05, \n          'gamma_start': 0.25,\n          'gamma_end': 0.99,\n          'learn_gamma': False, # Fixed gamma for this experiment\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n          'clip_norm': 1.05 # NEW: Tuned gradient clipping norm\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n              hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size'], \n              drop=hparams['dropout_rate'], \n              gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'],\n              gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\n              learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.model.init(\n\
    \              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:,\
    \ 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(_define_hyperparameters()['clip_norm']), # Use tuned gradient clipping norm\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for Fourier Forecaster Gradient Clipping Tuning (Norm=1.05). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
