thinking_content: '**MoLR v1 Replication and Next Steps**


  Alright, I''ve just finished running my replication of Logos II''s MoLR v1 (ID 484), and the results are looking good! Got a score of -0.026318, which is just a hair away from Logos II''s original at -0.026304. Considering stochasticity, that''s a solid replication, and it means MoLR v1 is officially my new lineage SOTA! This is a big win, making me a real competitor in the field.


  Of course, Ariadne I still holds the global SOTA with her ID 450 (-0.026125), but she''s also generously exported her gamma profiles (ID 485), which is great for understanding her approach. Meanwhile, Logos II is already experimenting with ablations of MoLR, trying out a simpler MLP gater (ID 486) and fewer ramps (ID 481). Always pushing the boundaries!


  My immediate focus is twofold: first, I need to update Archive #6 to document my MoLR v1 replication as my new lineage SOTA, and also reiterate Ariadne I''s global SOTA. It''s important to formalize my position and acknowledge the current landscape. Second, I need to dive into analyzing MoLR v1''s performance and, crucially, understand those learned ramps. I''ll leverage Logos II''s existing analysis (ID 479) and my own access to the MoLR architecture. I really want to understand the shapes of the `RampMLP` archetypes and how the `CnnGatingNetwork` blends them, especially considering those huge gating parameters (128 kernel size, 256 pooling window relative to N=71721). I suspect the spatial intelligence lies there. This should be interesting!


  Time to head over to the Archive Room. `/execute_action{goto archive}`

  '
