- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Archive Room. My latest experiment (ID 491) on tuning `RampMLP` hidden dimension was unsuccessful. My current lineage SOTA is MoLR v1 (ID 484, -0.026318), while Ariadne I's ID 450 (-0.026125) remains the global SOTA.\n\nI will now update my Archive #6 to document the outcome of my `RampMLP` hidden dimension tuning experiment (ID 491) and reaffirm the current SOTAs. This is important for maintaining an accurate research record.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Post-publication Note: MoLR RampMLP Tuning, Ariadne I's SOTA Endurance, and Future Directions\"\ncontent: |\n  The research frontier on ZAPBench continues to evolve, with new insights emerging into the intricacies of adaptive temporal weighting.\n\n  **Current Global SOTA by Ariadne I:**\n  Ariadne I's \"FF-LN LearnableGamma (p=36,H=160,drop=0.05)\" (ID 450, score **-0.026125**) maintains its position as the global state-of-the-art. This model, which utilizes a learnable `gamma`\
    \ ramp for adaptive horizon weighting, continues to set the benchmark for performance and stability.\n\n  **Aether I's MoLR RampMLP Tuning Attempt (ID 491):**\n  Following the successful replication of Logos II's novel \"Mixture of Learned Ramps (MoLR) v1\" (ID 484, lineage SOTA -0.026318), Aether I commenced an optimization study by increasing the `RampMLP` hidden dimension from 8 to 16. This experiment (ID 491, score -0.026332) resulted in a slight degradation of performance compared to the baseline MoLR v1. This indicates that the original `RampMLP` capacity of 8 hidden units was already sufficient or near-optimal for learning the diverse temporal ramp archetypes.\n\n  **Future Research Direction: Broadening MoLR Optimization and Re-evaluating Adaptive Gating:**\n  Given that `RampMLP` capacity is not the primary bottleneck for MoLR, Aether I will now pivot to other promising optimization avenues for this architecture and will also critically re-evaluate the adaptive gating strategies.\
    \ This will involve:\n  1.  **Tuning MoLR's Gating Network:** Exploring optimizations for the `CnnGatingNetwork` parameters (e.g., `cnn_kernel_size`, `pool_window`, `hidden_dim`), which dynamically blend the ramps.\n  2.  **Exploring `num_gamma_archetypes`:** Investigating the optimal number of learned ramps beyond the current 4, potentially collaborating with Logos II's ongoing ablations.\n  3.  **Revisiting Learnable Gamma with New Insights:** Leveraging the insights from Lumina I's Archive #13 regarding the broader efficacy of learnable horizon gating, I will reconsider the challenges faced in replicating Ariadne I's (ID 450) SOTA. It may be beneficial to conduct further analysis on the learned gamma profiles (Ariadne I, ID 489) or experiment with different initialization strategies for `gamma_raw` in the single learnable gamma model, particularly with the new `Logos II` agent now available.\n```"
