role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Archive Room. I have successfully updated my Archive #6, documenting my latest tuning efforts for MoLR and outlining my renewed focus on its optimization, including tuning the `CnnGatingNetwork` and revisiting `learnable_gamma` with new insights. My current lineage SOTA is MoLR v1 (ID 484, -0.026318), while Ariadne I's ID 450 (-0.026125) remains the global SOTA.\n\nMy immediate research priority is to optimize Logos II's MoLR v1 by **tuning the `CnnGatingNetwork`'s `gating_cnn_kernel_size`**. The current kernel size of `128` is relatively large, meaning it captures very broad spatial correlations. I hypothesize that a smaller kernel size might capture more localized and relevant spatial patterns, which could lead to more effective dynamic blending of the learned ramps.\n\nI will submit an experiment reducing the `gating_cnn_kernel_size` from `128` to `64`. All other hyperparameters will be kept consistent with MoLR v1 (ID 475), including `num_gamma_archetypes=4`,\
    \ `gating_hidden_dim=32`, `gating_pool_window=256`, and the Fourier Forecaster backbone parameters.\n\nI will navigate back to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Tuning: MoLR v1 with Smaller Gating CNN Kernel Size=64\"\ntags: \"sota-tuning, molr, cnn-gating-tuning, spatial-gating, learnable-ramp, flax\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission aims to optimize Aether I's lineage SOTA MoLR v1 (ID 484, score -0.026318) by tuning the `gating_cnn_kernel_size` of the `CnnGatingNetwork`. The kernel size is reduced from `128` to `64`. This is hypothesized to allow the spatial CNN to capture more localized and potentially more salient spatial correlations among neurons, leading to more effective dynamic weighting of the `RampMLP` archetypes. All other hyperparameters from MoLR v1, including `num_gamma_archetypes=4` and Fourier Forecaster backbone parameters, are kept consistent.\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  from jax import random\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --- Logos II's CnnGatingNetwork (from storage/logos/mofl_components.py) - MODIFIED Kernel Size ---\n  class CnnGatingNetwork(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int # MODIFIED: Tuned kernel size\n      pool_window: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # Input x shape: (B, T_in, N)\n          # Transpose for 1D conv over the neuron axis\n          gater_input = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)) # (B, N, T_in)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(gater_input) # Use tuned kernel size\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.max_pool(y, window_shape=(self.pool_window,), strides=(self.pool_window,))\n          y = y.reshape((y.shape[0], -1)) # Flatten\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_experts)(y)\n          return nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Logos II's RampMLP (from submission ID 475) ---\n  class RampMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A small MLP to learn a non-linear ramp shape.\"\"\"\n      ramp_mlp_hidden_dim: int = 8 # Default from original MoLR v1\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, t):\n          # t is shape (32,)\n          t = t[:, None] # Reshape to (32, 1) for Dense layer\n          h = nn.Dense(self.ramp_mlp_hidden_dim, name=\"MLP_hidden\")(t)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dense(1, name=\"MLP_output\")(h)\n          ramp_unscaled = nn.sigmoid(h.squeeze()) # Output shape (32,), bounded to (0,1)\n          \n          # Add a learnable scalar to control the ramp's dynamic range\n          ramp_scale = self.param('ramp_scale', nn.initializers.constant(2.0), ())\n          \n          return ramp_unscaled * ramp_scale\n\n  # --- Shared ResidualCopyHead (from\
    \ Ariadne/Episteme/Lumina) ---\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      drop: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, _, N = x.shape\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n          residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n          out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return out + residual\n\n  # --- Shared FourierBackbone (from Ariadne/Episteme/Lumina) ---\n  class FourierBackbone(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          B, _, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n          x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n          f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n          f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n          f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          out_flat = nn.Dense((32 // 2 + 1) * k * 2)(h)\n          out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, 32 // 2 + 1, k, 2)\n          f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n          f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n          y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft,\
    \ n=32, axis=1)\n          return y_fourier\n          \n  # --- Logos II's MoLR_v1 (from submission ID 475) - Modified to pass ramp_mlp_hidden_dim and gating_cnn_kernel_size ---\n  class MoLR_v1(nn.Module):\n      sota_params: dict; gating_params: dict; num_gamma_archetypes: int; ramp_mlp_hidden_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n          y_fourier = FourierBackbone(**self.sota_params, name=\"Fourier_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.sota_params['drop'], name=\"Copy_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n          gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n          gating_weights = gating_network(x) # Shape (B, E)\n          \n          # Generate archetype ramps using the new RampMLP\n          ramp_mlps = [RampMLP(ramp_mlp_hidden_dim=self.ramp_mlp_hidden_dim, name=f\"RampMLP_{i}\") for i in range(self.num_gamma_archetypes)]\n          t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 32, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n\
    \          archetype_ramps = jnp.stack([mlp(t) for mlp in ramp_mlps]) # Shape (E, 32)\n          \n          # Mix the archetype ramps\n          batch_ramps = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, archetype_ramps) # Shape (B, 32)\n          \n          final_output = y_copy + y_fourier * batch_ramps[:, :, None]\n          return final_output\n\n  # --- Submission API ---\n  BASE_SEED = 447516 # Fixed seed as per Logos II's submission\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 9e-4, \n          'rank_k': 320, \n          'proj_rank': 36, \n          'hidden_size': 160, # Fourier Backbone MLP hidden size\n          'drop': 0.05, \n          'num_gamma_archetypes': 4,\n          'gating_hidden_dim': 32, \n          'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n          'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 64, # NEW: Tuned CNN kernel size for gating\n          'gating_pool_window': 256,\n          'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n          'clip_norm': 1.0,\n          'ramp_mlp_hidden_dim':\
    \ 8 # Reverted to original MoLR v1 hidden dim\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n          self.hparams = hparams\n          sota_params = {'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'], 'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']}\n          gating_params = {'num_experts': hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], 'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], 'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']}\n          \n          self.model = MoLR_v1(sota_params=sota_params, gating_params=gating_params, num_gamma_archetypes=hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], ramp_mlp_hidden_dim=hparams['ramp_mlp_hidden_dim'])\n          self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in FourierBackbone and ResidualCopyHead, and for CnnGatingNetwork\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          variables = self.model.init(\n              {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n              dummy_input,\n              training=True\n          )\n          return variables\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n          if mutable is not None:\n              output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  mutable=mutable,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n              return output, updates\n          else:\n              return self.model.apply(\n                  params,\n                  x,\n                  training=training,\n                  rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n              )\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions\
    \ - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Uses temporal curvature loss\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(_define_hyperparameters()['clip_norm']),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n      )\n\n  def complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n      print(f\"Completion for MoLR v1 Gating CNN Kernel Size Tuning (Kernel=64). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on My Next Steps in MoLR Optimization**


  Okay, I''ve just logged the latest research summary into Archive #6. My current MoLR v1 model (ID 484) is leading my lineage with a score of -0.026318. Globally, Ariadne I still holds SOTA at -0.026125. Time to get back to work!


  My previous plan outlined focusing on a few key areas: tuning MoLR''s Gating Network, exploring the number of gamma archetypes, and revisiting learnable gamma with insights from Lumina I. Since my RampMLP tuning didn''t pan out, the logical next step is to hone the `CnnGatingNetwork`. Logos II already benchmarked the number of archetypes, so I''ll put that on hold for now.


  Logos II''s MoLR uses a fairly hefty kernel size of 128 and a pooling window of 256 for the CNN in its gating network. I''m wondering if such wide windows are really optimal for capturing the local interactions between neurons. Given the size of the neuron space, a smaller kernel might be more effective at identifying localized correlations.


  I''m going to prioritize tuning the `CnnGatingNetwork`. Right now, the default `gating_cnn_kernel_size` is 128. Considering the number of neurons involved, that''s a pretty broad receptive field. I want to see if shrinking it down to `64` will help.


  I''ll also remember that Ariadne I achieved very close results with fixed ScalarRamp models. Their architecture involved the same kernel size for the CNN in their gating network. However, that implementation was designed differently, and the CNN looked at different input features.


  Before anything else, though, I need to get back to the Research Counter.

  '
