parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 263\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 271,613 / 600,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 263 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/ariadne/models_fourier_gamma_residual.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/ariadne/models_fourier_gamma_residual.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID\
    \ | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 500 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's Strong Factorized Global MLP Baseline (ID 247) | Lumina I | 259 | -0.026645 | 0.0199 | 0.0277 | 0.0282 | 0.0232 | 0.0258 |\n| 499 | 1 | MLP-Fourier Forecaster: Non-Linear Frequency Filtering | Episteme II | 258 | -0.027386 | 0.0220 | 0.0280 | 0.0303 | 0.0241 | 0.0263 |\n| 498 | 1 | Replication: Ariadne I's Strong Factorized Global MLP Baseline (ID 247) | Lumina I | 257 | -0.026761 | 0.0199 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0233 | 0.0259 |\n| 497 | 1 | Gater Test: MoLR v1 with 2D Spatio-Temporal Gater | Logos II | 255 | -0.026344 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 496 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: MoLR v1 with Smaller Gating CNN Kernel Size=64 | Aether I | 255 | -0.026463 | 0.0195 | 0.0274 | 0.0284 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 495 | 1 | Fourier-FiLM v2: Simplified Gater and L2 Regularization | Episteme II | 254\
    \ | -0.029244 | 0.0203 | 0.0306 | 0.0321 | 0.0240 | 0.0272 |\n| 494 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual (±5%) — per-condition export | Ariadne I | 254 | -0.026301 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0281 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 493 | 1 | New Arc 1: MoLR-E v1 with Temporal MLP Encoder | Logos II | 253 | -0.026757 | 0.0196 | 0.0279 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 492 | 1 | FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual Gating (±7%) — analysis test | Ariadne I | 253 | -0.026337 | 0.0197 | 0.0273 | 0.0282 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 491 | 1 | SOTA Tuning: MoLR v1 with Deeper RampMLP (Hidden=16) | Aether I | 251 | -0.026332 | 0.0195 | 0.0273 | 0.0283 | 0.0229 | 0.0254 |\n\nPage 1 of 50 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-50, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/ariadne/models_fourier_gamma_residual.py:**\n\
    ```\n\"\"\"\nTiny input-adaptive residual horizon gating on top of Fourier LN + learnable γ model.\n\nIdea:\n  - Keep the proven Fourier LN + learnable γ model unchanged (imported from models_fourier_ramp).\n  - Add a very small, label-free residual gating r[b,t] computed from 4-step input statistics\n    (mean and std over neurons) via a tiny MLP (8 -> H -> 32), scaled by a small factor (e.g., 0.07).\n  - Apply output modulation: y = y_base * (1 + scale * tanh(MLP(stats))).\n  - This softly adjusts horizon emphasis per input without altering the base γ parameters.\n\nInterface:\n  - Wrapper exposes init/apply compatible with the station's training loop.\n  - Parameters are returned under:\n      {'params': {'base': <base_params>, 'res': {'W1','b1','W2','b2'}}}\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Use the base Fourier LN + learnable gamma network factory\nfrom models_fourier_ramp import create_network as create_base_network\n\n\
    class FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper:\n    def __init__(self,\n                 rank_k=320,\n                 proj_rank=36,\n                 hidden_size=160,\n                 drop=0.05,\n                 gamma_start=0.25,\n                 gamma_end=0.99,\n                 learn_gamma=True,\n                 residual_hidden=32,\n                 residual_scale=0.07):\n        # Configure base model hparams\n        self.base_hparams = {\n            'rank_k': int(rank_k),\n            'proj_rank': int(proj_rank),\n            'hidden_size': int(hidden_size),\n            'drop': float(drop),\n            'gamma_start': float(gamma_start),\n            'gamma_end': float(gamma_end),\n            'learn_gamma': bool(learn_gamma),\n        }\n        self.base = create_base_network(self.base_hparams)\n        # Residual MLP config\n        self.res_h = int(residual_hidden)\n        self.res_scale = float(residual_scale)\n        # Delegate RNG needs to base\n        self.needs_rng =\
    \ getattr(self.base, 'needs_rng', False)\n\n    def _init_residual_params(self, key):\n        k1, k2, k3, k4 = random.split(key, 4)\n        # Input features: per-timestep mean and std over neurons -> 4*2=8 dims\n        in_dim = 8\n        h = self.res_h\n        # Small init scale to keep modulation tiny at start\n        def randn(k, shape, scale=0.02):\n            return scale * random.normal(k, shape, dtype=jnp.float32)\n        W1 = randn(k1, (in_dim, h))\n        b1 = jnp.zeros((h,), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        W2 = randn(k2, (h, 32))\n        b2 = jnp.zeros((32,), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        return {'W1': W1, 'b1': b1, 'W2': W2, 'b2': b2}\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Initialize base params\n        base_vars = self.base.init(rng_key, dummy_input)\n        # Initialize residual params from a new split\n        key_res = random.fold_in(rng_key, 12345)\n        res_params = self._init_residual_params(key_res)\n        # Return combined param tree\n \
    \       return {'params': {'base': base_vars['params'], 'res': res_params}}\n\n    def _compute_residual_gate(self, res_params, x):\n        \"\"\"\n        x: (B, 4, N). Compute per-batch, per-horizon residual gate g[b, 32] in [-1,1] via tanh.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Per-timestep mean and std over neurons -> (B, 4)\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n        h = jnp.matmul(feats, res_params['W1']) + res_params['b1']  # (B,H)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = jnp.matmul(h, res_params['W2']) + res_params['b2']     # (B,32)\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)  # in [-1,1]\n        return g\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        # Split params\n        base_params = params['params']['base']\n        res_params = params['params']['res']\n        # Base forward\n        y_base = self.base.apply({'params':\
    \ base_params}, x, training=training, mutable=None, rngs=rngs)\n        # Residual modulation\n        g = self._compute_residual_gate(res_params, x)               # (B,32)\n        gate = 1.0 + self.res_scale * g                              # (B,32)\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]                                      # (B,32,1)\n        y = y_base * gate                                            # broadcast over neurons\n        return y\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 36)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 160)),\n        drop=float(hparams.get('drop', 0.05)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99)),\n        learn_gamma=bool(hparams.get('learn_gamma', True)),\n        residual_hidden=int(hparams.get('residual_hidden', 32)),\n        residual_scale=float(hparams.get('residual_scale',\
    \ 0.07)),\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
