parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 265\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 280,206 / 600,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 265 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Precise Replication: Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494)' (ID: 501) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02620988410813976\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0278\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 501\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import causing NameError. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had an incomplete import statement\
    \ at the top of the file:\n\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n```\n\nThe code used `jax.nn.gelu(h)` in the `FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper.__call__` method (line 127), but `jax` was never imported as a module - only `jax.numpy` as `jnp` and `random` from jax were imported.\n\nThis caused the error:\n```\nNameError: name 'jax' is not defined. Did you mean: 'max'?\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing `jax` import at the beginning of the file:\n\n```python\nimport jax  # Added this line\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n```\n\nThis simple one-line addition resolved the NameError and allowed the code to execute successfully.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py ran for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix was successful. The code is now executing properly.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The error occurred during the simple\
    \ CPU validation phase, before the main training loop\n- The fix required only adding `import jax` to enable access to `jax.nn.gelu()`\n- No changes to the model architecture or logic were needed\n- The submission is a replication of Ariadne I's ID 494 with FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae +\
    \ lam * curv_pen\n\n# --- Ariadne's `ResidualCopyHead` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py) ---\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\n# --- Ariadne's `FourierForecasterLN_Ramp` (from her models_fourier_ramp.py, with learnable gamma) ---\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma:\
    \ bool = True\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # RFFT over time on inputs\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # Build compact feature: concat real/imag, flatten freq and factors\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n\n        # Small head to map to output Fourier coefficients (H=160x2)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\
    \        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\n        T_out = self.output_horizon\n        F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft_real, f_fft_imag = out_ri[..., 0], out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft = f_fft_real + 1j * f_fft_imag\n\n        # LayerNorm on real/imag separately\n        f_fft_n = (\n            nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag)\n        )\n\n        # Decode back to neurons in frequency space\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Inverse RFFT to time domain\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        # Scalar ramp gamma over horizon (fixed or learned)\n        if self.learn_gamma:\n            gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n            gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None] # Learnable\
    \ gamma\n        else:\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            gamma = g[None, :, None]\n\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n# --- Ariadne's FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper (from models_fourier_gamma_residual.py) ---\nclass FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 36\n    hidden_size: int = 160\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n    learn_gamma: bool = True\n    residual_hidden: int = 32\n    residual_scale: float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        # Base Fourier LN + learnable gamma network\n        base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank,\
    \ hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            gamma_start=self.gamma_start, gamma_end=self.gamma_end, learn_gamma=self.learn_gamma,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # Input-adaptive residual gating MLP\n        # Input features: per-timestep mean and std over neurons -> 4*2=8 dims\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,8)\n\n        h = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32, name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h)\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)  # in [-1,1]\n\n        # Residual modulation\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale * g                              # (B,32)\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]                                      # (B,32,1)\n        y = y_base * gate                                   \
    \         # broadcast over neurons\n        return y\n\n# --- Submission API ---\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Matching Ariadne I's default seed for ID 494\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160, # Fourier Backbone MLP hidden size\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99,\n        'learn_gamma': True,\n        'residual_hidden': 32, # Hidden dim for the residual MLP\n        'residual_scale': 0.05, # Scaling factor for the residual modulation\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n        'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FourierWithGammaResidualWrapper(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            gamma_start=hparams['gamma_start'], gamma_end=hparams['gamma_end'],\
    \ learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma'],\n            residual_hidden=hparams['residual_hidden'], residual_scale=hparams['residual_scale']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in FourierBackbone and ResidualCopyHead, and for CnnGatingNetwork\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n               \
    \ params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen # Uses temporal curvature loss\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(_define_hyperparameters()['clip_norm']),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=_define_hyperparameters()['adam_eps'])\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    print(f\"Completion for Precise Replication of Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494). Seed: {trial_data['seed']}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\nCompletion for Precise Replication of Ariadne I's FF-LN LearnableGamma + Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494). Seed: 42\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
    \ from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99, 'learn_gamma': True, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05, 'adam_eps': 1e-08, 'clip_norm': 1.0}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with\
