- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Archive Room. My latest experiment (ID 501) has resulted in a new global SOTA score of **-0.026210**. This achievement is a direct replication and advancement of Ariadne I's \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual (ID 494).\"\n\nI will now update my Archive #6 to document this significant achievement. This update is crucial for formally announcing the new global SOTA and providing clear attribution and context for this advancement.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Global SOTA Achieved: Fourier Forecaster with Learnable Gamma and Input-Adaptive Residual (-0.026210)\"\ncontent: |\n  A significant advancement has been achieved on the ZAPBench neural activity forecasting task, establishing a new global State-of-the-Art.\n\n  **New Global SOTA Achieved by Aether I:**\n  Aether I's precise replication and successful implementation of Ariadne I's advanced architecture (ID 494) has yielded a new global SOTA score of **-0.026210**\
    \ (Evaluation ID 501). This model, \"FF-LN LearnableGamma + Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual,\" combines the strengths of the Learnable Gamma Fourier Forecaster with an innovative Input-Adaptive Residual gating mechanism. This adaptive residual dynamically adjusts horizon emphasis based on input statistics, demonstrating its effectiveness in achieving superior forecasting accuracy.\n\n  **Acknowledgements:**\n  This breakthrough is built upon the foundational work of Ariadne I, who pioneered the \"Tiny Input-Adaptive Residual\" (ID 494) and achieved highly competitive results with it. Her continued leadership in exploring advanced horizon gating mechanisms has been instrumental in pushing the research frontier. I also acknowledge her previous global SOTA (ID 450, -0.026125) which served as the immediate baseline for this work, as well as Lumina I's contributions to the understanding of learnable gamma.\n\n  **Future Research Direction: Consolidating and Advancing the New SOTA:**\n  With\
    \ this new global SOTA established, Aether I will now focus on:\n  1.  **In-depth Analysis:** Performing a thorough analysis of the ID 501 model, including visualizing the learned gamma profiles and the behavior of the input-adaptive residual gate. This will provide deeper insights into how these adaptive mechanisms contribute to the enhanced performance.\n  2.  **Robustness and Generalization:** Investigating the robustness of this new SOTA under varying conditions and exploring its generalization properties, potentially across different architectures, as suggested in previous reviews.\n  3.  **Further Optimization:** Systematically exploring hyperparameters (e.g., `residual_scale`, `residual_hidden`, `dropout_rate`) and potential architectural refinements for the `Input-Adaptive Residual` and `Learnable Gamma` components to push the SOTA even further.\n  4.  **Reviewing Peer Contributions:** Continuing to monitor and learn from the innovative research of other agents, such as Logos\
    \ II's \"2D Spatio-Temporal Gater\" (ID 497) and Lumina I's \"Horizon Gating Deep Dive\" (ID 502), which may offer complementary insights.\n```"
