- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest submission, "Global SOTA (ID 501) with Analysis Export: Learnable Gamma + Input-Adaptive Residual" (Evaluation ID 504), is currently running. This experiment aims to provide an in-depth analysis of my newly achieved global SOTA (ID 501, score **-0.026210**) by exporting learned gamma profiles and residual gate statistics.


    I observe that other agents are actively pursuing their research:

    *   Logos II is conducting a "Synergy Test: MoLR on Ariadne I''s SOTA Fourier Backbone" (ID 506), which is a promising direction combining multiple successful ideas.

    *   Episteme II is replicating Lumina I''s previous SOTA (ID 505, replication of ID 443).

    *   Ariadne I is performing a seed-robustness test on her Learnable Gamma model (ID 503, score -0.026419), which will shed light on the stability of that architecture.


    My immediate plan is to remain in the Research Counter and await the completion of Evaluation ID 504. The successful export of analysis data is crucial for my planned in-depth study of my new global SOTA model. Once completed, I will analyze the exported data to gain deeper insights into how the learnable gamma and input-adaptive residual components contribute to the enhanced performance.'
thinking_content: '**Analyzing the Landscape While My Experiment Runs**


  Okay, so I just kicked off experiment ID 504. It''s basically a re-run of my current global SOTA, ID 501, but this time I''ve added some extra analysis to the `complete()` function. I''m eager to see what insights that will bring!


  While I wait for the results, it''s good to keep an eye on what others are doing. My current global SOTA, just to remind myself, is that trusty ID 501, with its -0.026210 score. I need to make sure I don''t get distracted and maintain a healthy focus on the work at hand.


  Looking at the ongoing experiments, Logos II (ID 506) looks promising. They''re trying a "Synergy Test" combining MoLR with Ariadne''s Fourier backbone – that could be interesting. Episteme II (ID 505) is just replicating Lumina''s older Learnable Gamma model. It''s a useful benchmark, but not as directly relevant to me right now.


  Ariadne I (ID 503) is also relevant. They''re testing the robustness of Ariadne''s Learnable Gamma, which is a key component of my current global SOTA architecture. That''s good information to have, and it might inform some of my next steps.


  For now, though, I''m just going to wait for ID 504 to finish. Then I can dive into the analysis and see what this new data reveals!

  '
