parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 278\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 343,729 / 600,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 278 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 513**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Innovation: Learned Non-Linear Gamma via Tiny MLP\n**ID:** 513\n**Tags:** sota-innovation, learnable-gamma, non-linear, parsimony\n**Abstract:** Building on my successful replication of Ariadne I's SOTA (ID 508), this experiment tests a single, parsimonious innovation. I hypothesize that the SOTA's simple learnable vector of per-horizon weights (`gamma_raw`) can be improved by replacing it with a more expressive, non-linear function. To test this, I have replaced the `gamma_raw` parameter with a tiny MLP (`t(1) -> MLP(8) -> output(1)`) that learns\
    \ a non-linear mapping from the normalized timestep to the pre-sigmoid gamma value. All other aspects of the SOTA architecture and hyperparameters are preserved. This is a controlled test to see if a more expressive, learned non-linear horizon weighting\n**Score:** -0.02639949892620953\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0274\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0283\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n\nclass GammaMLP(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, t):\n        t = t[:, None] # Reshape for Dense layer\n        h = nn.Dense(8, name=\"MLP_hidden\")(t); h = nn.relu(h)\n        gamma_raw = nn.Dense(1, name=\"MLP_output\")(h)\n        return gamma_raw.squeeze()\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x,\
    \ training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float; output_horizon: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft,\
    \ (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        T_out = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n\n        # --- My Innovation ---\n        # Replace learnable vector with a tiny MLP\n        t_coords = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T_out, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n\
    \        gamma_raw = GammaMLP(name=\"Gamma_MLP\")(t_coords)\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        # --- End Innovation ---\n\n        y_fourier_ramped = gamma * y_fourier\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_copy + y_fourier_ramped\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Matching my successful SOTA replication (ID 508)\n\
    \    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return Wrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute\
    \ loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 554306 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 554308\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.033461   |   0.029391  \n   2    |   0.029137   |   0.029327  \n   3    |   0.028965   |   0.029294  \n   4    |   0.028884   |   0.029188  \n   5    |   0.028838   |   0.029232  \n   6    |   0.028810   |   0.029124  \n   7    |   0.028776   |   0.029186  \n   8    |   0.028737   |   0.028963  \n   9    |   0.028543   |   0.028660  \n  10    |   0.028365   |   0.028521  \n  11    |   0.028173   |   0.028376  \n \
    \ 12    |   0.027914   |   0.028764  \n  13    |   0.027723   |   0.027887  \n  14    |   0.027556   |   0.027924  \n  15    |   0.027469   |   0.028021  \n  16    |   0.027260   |   0.027581  \n  17    |   0.027104   |   0.027996  \n  18    |   0.026897   |   0.027401  \n  19    |   0.026721   |   0.027219  \n  20    |   0.026588   |   0.027034  \n  21    |   0.026509   |   0.027103  \n  22    |   0.026350   |   0.026809  \n  23    |   0.026194   |   0.027098  \n  24    |   0.026108   |   0.026719  \n  25    |   0.025977   |   0.026926  \n  26    |   0.025943   |   0.027017  \n  27    |   0.025805   |   0.026622  \n  28    |   0.025790   |   0.026866  \n  29    |   0.025698   |   0.026777  \n  30    |   0.025603   |   0.026462  \n  31    |   0.025546   |   0.026568  \n  32    |   0.025520   |   0.026664  \n  33    |   0.025395   |   0.026588  \n  34    |   0.025368   |   0.026546  \n  35    |   0.025286   |   0.026416  \n  36    |   0.025247   |   0.026701  \n  37    |   0.025180  \
    \ |   0.026604  \n  38    |   0.025097   |   0.026834  \n  39    |   0.025081   |   0.026466  \n  40    |   0.025022   |   0.026594  \n  41    |   0.024983   |   0.026749  \n  42    |   0.024965   |   0.026769  \n  43    |   0.024879   |   0.026571  \n  44    |   0.024858   |   0.026845  \n  45    |   0.024835   |   0.026754  \n  46    |   0.024773   |   0.026583  \n  47    |   0.024788   |   0.026620  \n  48    |   0.024690   |   0.026732  \n  49    |   0.024668   |   0.026725  \n  50    |   0.024636   |   0.026713  \n  51    |   0.024590   |   0.026992  \n  52    |   0.024561   |   0.026925  \n  53    |   0.024541   |   0.026817  \n  54    |   0.024512   |   0.026672  \n  55    |   0.024490   |   0.026803  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 55 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2498.3s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026416\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026416\nTraining time: 2510s\n\nStarting ZAPBench\
