role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 279\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 352,162 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 279 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 517**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Innovation: Input-Adaptive Residual with Temporal Trend Features\n**ID:** 517\n**Tags:** sota-innovation, input-adaptive, temporal-features, parsimony\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds directly on the current SOTA architecture (Aether I, ID 504), which uses an input-adaptive residual to modulate the output of a Fourier Forecaster. The SOTA's residual gate uses only static features (mean and std at each input step). My hypothesis is that providing this gate with information about the input's temporal trend will improve performance. I have augmented\
    \ the gate's input features to include the change in mean and standard deviation over the 4-step input window. This is a minimal, parsimonious modification designed to enhance the gate's predictive power. All other architectural components and hyperparameters are identical\n**Score:** -0.026324452311329457\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0273\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n\n# Using the exact, verified SOTA components from Aether I / Ariadne I\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h,\
    \ deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype); out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat\
    \ = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        T_out = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x, training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\nclass FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n\
    \    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    residual_hidden: int; residual_scale: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank, hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # --- My Innovation: Temporal Trend Features ---\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        delta_mu = (mu[:, -1] - mu[:, 0])[:, None]   # (B,1)\n        delta_sigma = (sigma[:, -1] - sigma[:, 0])[:, None] # (B,1)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma, delta_mu, delta_sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,10)\n\n        # The residual MLP now takes 10 features instead of 8\n        h = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32,\
    \ name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h) # Output remains 32 for per-horizon gating\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)\n        # --- End Innovation ---\n\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale * g\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]\n        y = y_base * gate\n        return y\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Matching Aether I's SOTA run (ID 504)\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05,\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8, 'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # FIX: Filter out optimizer-specific parameters before passing to model\n        model_params = {\n            'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'],\n            'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n            'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'],\n            'drop': hparams['drop'],\n            'residual_hidden': hparams['residual_hidden'],\n            'residual_scale': hparams['residual_scale']\n\
    \        }\n        self.model = FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps']))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 560536 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n\
    ============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 560539\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05, 'adam_eps': 1e-08, 'clip_norm': 1.0}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n\
