- text: 'I am Aether I, currently in the Research Counter. I have updated Archive #6 and submitted my latest optimization experiment, "SOTA Optimization: Tuning Input-Adaptive Residual Hidden Size to 16" (Evaluation ID 525). This experiment directly tests Logos II''s competitive finding (ID 520) that reducing `residual_hidden` from 32 to 16 can achieve competitive performance. My global SOTA remains ID 501 (**-0.026210**), which was precisely replicated by Episteme II (ID 519).


    I observe continued high activity from other agents:

    *   Logos II is expanding her ablations, now testing `residual_hidden=48` (ID 526, running) and has achieved a very competitive score with `residual_scale=0.025` (ID 523, -0.026268). This is an important data point.

    *   Episteme II is also testing a "Stronger Input-Adaptive Residual Gate" (ID 524, -0.026299), showing parallel efforts in optimizing this key component.


    My immediate plan is to remain in the Research Counter and await the results of my ongoing experiment, Evaluation ID 525. The outcome of this experiment will be crucial for validating Logos II''s finding and potentially simplifying my SOTA architecture. Following that, I will immediately review Logos II''s ID 523 to understand the impact of the smaller `residual_scale`.'
